window.DOC_CONTENT = ["# 鲁琨｜制造业外企职场英语学习路线\n\n制定日期：2026-10-25。基础：CET-4 528、CET-6 478；统计学本科；目标方向：项目管理/PMO、数据分析；每天约90分钟。\n\n## 1. 目标与安排\n\n四六级成绩作为背景信息，不直接换算成口语或工作英语等级。先用02文件测出实际短板，再分配训练时间。\n\n采用12周路线，每周6天、每天90分钟，共108小时；周日休息或自愿花10分钟整理。前2周优先支持秋招面试，前8周完成核心场景，第9—12周练习陌生任务和跨部门协作。若2026-10-26开始，第2周结束于11月8日，第4周结束于11月22日，第8周结束于12月20日，第12周结束于2027年1月17日。课程日期可整体平移。\n\n训练目标是能独立完成可检查的工作任务。以下是学习目标，不是外企统一录用门槛，也不承诺在固定时间达到某个CEFR等级。\n\n| 节点 | 可检查的目标 |\n|---|---|\n| 第2周 | 不照稿做60—90秒自我介绍；讲述2段真实经历；应对3个英文追问；15分钟完成一封基本完整的英文邮件 |\n| 第4周 | 做2分钟项目状态汇报；说明风险、责任人、日期；用12分钟写清请求邮件或会议跟进邮件 |\n| 第8周 | 做3分钟数据汇报并回答3个追问；准确表达分母、单位、百分比/百分点；完成10分钟业务角色对话 |\n| 第12周 | 在综合模拟中完成会议理解、数据说明、风险沟通、邮件闭环；完成20分钟英文模拟面试 |\n\n项目管理与数据分析先共用约60%的内容，其余各占20%。拿到明确JD后，把分支时间调整为目标岗位30%、另一方向10%。暂不以产品经理作为这里的PM训练方向。\n\n## 2. 核心能力地图\n\n| 能力 | 项目管理/PMO练什么 | 数据分析练什么 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 听 | 听出变更、责任人、期限、未决事项 | 听懂指标定义、业务问题、分析请求 |\n| 说 | 状态—风险—影响—行动—请求 | 结论—证据—解释—限制—建议 |\n| 读 | 任务表、会议纪要、交付与验证要求 | 指标说明、图表、数据质量说明 |\n| 写 | 进度更新、催办、升级、会议纪要 | 分析摘要、数据请求、异常说明 |\n| 互动 | 澄清模糊安排、确认承诺、协商资源 | 核实口径、解释异常、回答质疑 |\n\n所有练习优先使用制造业场景：样件交付、供应商延期、验证排期、物料短缺、产量、质量、返工、库存、交付及时率。工作区既有汽车项目/PMO材料可以提供任务类型；个人面试故事只使用你能证明的实际动作和结果。\n\n## 3. 每天90分钟怎么练\n\n| 时间 | 训练 | 必须留下的产物 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 15分钟 | 听1—3分钟材料：不看字幕听主旨，再听细节，最后查原文 | 3—5条英文要点；听错的数字/日期 |\n| 10分钟 | 选其中30—60秒跟读；录音后对照 | 1段录音；标出影响理解的发音 |\n| 25分钟 | 当天主任务：角色对话、项目更新、数据汇报或面试 | 1次不照稿口头输出 |\n| 25分钟 | 写作：邮件、分析摘要、会议行动项 | 首稿+修改稿；标明用时 |\n| 10分钟 | 从当天任务提取5个表达，替换对象/数字再用 | 5张表达卡，复习旧卡 |\n| 5分钟 | 记录3个错误、1个明日重点 | 训练日志 |\n\n25分钟口语块可拆为：3分钟列英文关键词、4分钟首轮表达、5分钟追问、5分钟反馈、5分钟重说、3分钟记录。不要先写完整中文再翻译整篇。\n\n周六把90分钟改为：45分钟陌生任务小测+30分钟订正/重说+15分钟更新记录。第4、8、12周周六改为60分钟综合测试+30分钟订正。\n\n忙碌日的30分钟保底：8分钟盲听、10分钟开口、10分钟短邮件、2分钟记录。漏练后正常继续，不一次补做数小时。\n\n## 4. 12周任务安排\n\n每周产出基准：3段录音、2封邮件、1份短业务文档、1次测试。日常训练可以重复修改同一篇作品，不追求每天换题。\n\n| 周次 | 场景和训练重点 | 周末交付/测试 |\n|---|---|---|\n| W1 | 起点测评；自我介绍；说明统计学背景与岗位关联；基础邮件 | 60秒自我介绍；1段真实经历；初测记录 |\n| W2 | 秋招面试；项目/分析经历；why this role；追问个人贡献、困难、结果 | 10分钟模拟面试；2段真实STAR故事；安排/跟进邮件 |\n| W3 | 项目周会：里程碑、状态、依赖、责任人、到期日 | 2分钟项目更新；英文行动项表；延误说明 |\n| W4 | 邮件往来：询问信息、催办、延期、升级、纪要 | 首次综合复测；3轮邮件链；按错误调整W5—8 |\n| W5 | 数据汇报：产量、缺陷、交付；趋势、对比、分母、单位 | 2分钟图表说明；120词分析摘要；数字准确性测试 |\n| W6 | 数据请求与质量：缺失、重复、口径、时间窗口、连接问题 | 向业务方提5个澄清问题；数据请求邮件；解释一个异常 |\n| W7 | 制造业协作：供应商延期、物料短缺、验证排期、产能约束 | 10分钟跨部门模拟；风险升级邮件；恢复计划 |\n| W8 | 综合任务：读业务简报→说明数据→主持讨论→发纪要 | 第二次综合复测；3分钟汇报+3个追问；选择主攻方向 |\n| W9 | 读真实制造业案例；复述业务问题、方案、证据 | 250—500词案例阅读；90秒复述；5个术语解释 |\n| W10 | 提出建议、礼貌异议、协商优先级；PM练资源，DA练证据 | 一次意见分歧对话；100—150词建议；更换陌生题材 |\n| W11 | 对准具体JD、公司产品和英文面试；限时书面任务 | 20分钟模拟面试；现场英文邮件/分析摘要；盲抽题 |\n| W12 | 独立综合交付；识别剩余短板；制定后续月计划 | 最终复测；与首测逐维度比较；整理个人表达库 |\n\n## 5. 第一周逐日计划\n\n第一天：做02文件60分钟初测；再用约15分钟做British Council在线语法词汇测评；15分钟整理错误和保存答案。\n\n第二天：用B1口语栏目“Meeting face-to-face”练介绍；录60秒自我介绍；写80—100词给新同事的介绍邮件。内容只用真实信息。\n\n第三天：选一段真实项目经历，列角色、目标、动作、结果；讲90秒；回答“What exactly did you do?”；写5条项目状态要点。\n\n第四天：学English for emails中的Starting and finishing emails、Making arrangements；写会议邀请邮件；口头协商一个时间；重复数字和时区确认。\n\n第五天：用04文件的模拟数据做90秒汇报；准确说产量完成率、缺陷率、交付变化；写100词摘要；解释3%到4%的变化。\n\n第六天：45分钟小测（面试15、陌生邮件15、陌生数据说明15）；30分钟纠错重做；15分钟回顾。测试题由伙伴或AI当场改变信息，避免背模板得分。\n\n周日：休息；可选整理10分钟。\n\n## 6. 学习网站：控制在少量主资源\n\n以下页面于2026-10-25核验。网页可检索不代表已验证你本地网络的音视频播放；若播放器受限，先用同站其他音频，不以阅读原文代替听力成绩。\n\n| 资源 | 定位与难度 | 使用频率与方式 |\n|---|---|---|\n| [British Council在线测评](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/english-levels/online-english-level-test) | 语法、词汇和措辞的粗略定位；需免费账号 | 起点做一次，记录结果；不能据此判断口语/会议水平 |\n| [B1 Speaking](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking/b1) | 有视频、可重复的表达和练习 | 每周2次；先练Meeting face-to-face、Agreeing and disagreeing；看后换成工厂/项目场景 |\n| [English for emails](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/business/english-emails) | A2—B1，组织邮件、询问、安排、校对 | W1—4每周2单元左右；完成练习后写自己的业务邮件 |\n| [B2 Listening](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b2) | 音频、练习、原文 | 每周2—3篇；A design presentation、A business interview等见02文件，测试保留篇目不要提前练 |\n| [Podcasts for professionals](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/business-english/podcasts-professionals) | B2，业务对话和演讲，附练习和原文 | W5起每周1篇；先练Managing conflict、Change management |\n| [Cambridge Write & Improve](https://writeandimprove.com/) | 基础写作练习与自动反馈免费，另有付费模块 | 每周2篇；独立首稿→查看反馈→自己修改→说明改动；业务信息是否完整需另查 |\n| [Siemens制造业案例](https://www.siemens.com/en-us/company/software-case-studies/) | 未分级真实业务材料 | W9起每周1个；只读250—500词，提取problem/action/result；供应商案例中的成果归因需辨别 |\n\n可从[NAF质量管理案例](https://resources.sw.siemens.com/en-GB/case-study-naf/)开始，选Challenges、Keys to success、Results及少量正文，练“质量问题—系统整合—业务影响”的说明。无需先学会其中的软件。\n\n不必一开始购买课程。若连续两周在同一口语维度停滞，可安排有反馈的真人模拟；把具体邮件和场景带去，而非仅自由聊天。\n\n## 7. 测试与调整规则\n\n初测和W4/W8/W12复测均分为：听力20、阅读15、邮件25、口头汇报25、互动15。详见02、03文件。总分是本计划内部练习分，不能换算成四六级、雅思、CEFR或企业合格线。\n\n每周测试记录：独立完成用时、关键信息遗漏、数字错误、需要重复/澄清次数、长停顿次数。把原稿与修改稿分开；同一道题修改后进步不等于陌生任务迁移。\n\n复测目标：W4争取70分且五个分项均不低于满分的50%；W8争取80分且分项均不低于60%；W12争取80分且分项均不低于70%，同时能在陌生任务中完成闭环。分数目标为训练决策规则。\n\n听力难度选择：初测先做B2。完成Task 1、2后正确率低于40%，下次使用B1，不在当天先看原文再测。正确率40%—79%继续相同级别；连续两次陌生材料达到80%后适度增加语速、篇幅或口音变化，每次只改一项。不同材料不完全等难，须同时看任务完成情况。\n\n若听力持续薄弱：把日常90分钟改为听力25、跟读10、口语20、写作20、表达10、记录5。若听力尚可但口语卡顿：听力10、跟读10、口语35、写作20、表达10、记录5。邮件薄弱时：听力10、跟读10、口语20、写作35、表达10、记录5。每两周只主攻最弱的一项，再复测。\n\n## 8. 用AI练习的约定\n\n练习模式允许查词、看示范、听原文、反复修改；测试模式先独立完成，关闭翻译和自动改写，结束后才反馈。\n\n发音、流畅度和实际听力需要音频证据。只有文字时，只评内容与语言组织，口语相关分项写“未测”，不凑成100分。AI反馈可用于练习，不替代正式能力认证。\n\n如果对话工具支持语音，可以用语音做角色扮演；只有文字功能时，先录音再由真人或可处理音频的工具反馈。文本角色扮演仍可训练措辞和澄清逻辑。\n\n每次只修正最影响理解的3个问题，修完重新输出。使用模拟或脱敏材料，不把客户、供应商和内部业务细节直接上传公共练习网站。\n\n## 9. 每周记录模板\n\n| 周次/日期 | 实际分钟 | 听力材料/级别/正确率 | 录音题目与时长 | 邮件用时/遗漏 | 互动情况 | 三个反复错误 | 下周唯一重点 |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 起点 | | | | | | | |\n| W1 | | | | | | | |\n| W2 | | | | | | | |\n| W3 | | | | | | | |\n| W4复测 | | | | | | | |\n| W5 | | | | | | | |\n| W6 | | | | | | | |\n| W7 | | | | | | | |\n| W8复测 | | | | | | | |\n| W9 | | | | | | | |\n| W10 | | | | | | | |\n| W11 | | | | | | | |\n| W12复测 | | | | | | | |\n\n建议保存：日期_任务_首稿、日期_任务_修改稿、日期_任务_录音。最终积累的是可迁移的表达和可见的进步，不只是网站访问记录。\n","# 起点测试与阶段复测｜考生版\n\n对象：统计学背景，制造业外企项目管理/数据分析方向。所有工厂、人物、数字与业务安排均为虚构练习材料，不代表真实雇主或个人经历。\n\n总计60分钟，满分100分。顺序：听力12分钟→阅读8分钟→邮件18分钟→口头汇报12分钟→互动10分钟。测试前不读03文件。查词、翻译、AI生成、自动改写在测试阶段关闭；测试后可以使用。\n\n需要：计时器、录音设备、空白文档、音频播放器。若没有口语评估者，先保存录音，口语和互动暂不评分；若互动用文字完成，标注为“文本互动练习”，不与语音互动分直接比较。\n\n## A. 听力｜20分｜12分钟\n\n起点使用：[A design presentation，B2](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b2/design-presentation)。这是一篇产品设计与推出计划的听力。\n\n1. 可以先看Task 1、Task 2的题目，不做Preparation词汇练习。\n2. 收起或遮住Transcript区域，不滚动阅读原文。最多播放2遍，原速，不逐句暂停。\n3. 独立完成页面的Task 1、Task 2；在查看答案前保存所有答案。\n4. 完成后才对照答案，记C为答对小题数、N为全部小题数。听力得分=20×C/N，保留1位小数。记录第一次/第二次播放各理解了什么。\n5. 超时停止，未答题计错。网页无法播放时本项记“未测”，不要用阅读文字替代。\n\n起点得分低于8/20时，下次改用[B1：A team meeting about diversity](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b1/team-meeting-about-diversity)，按相同规则测。分别记录级别，不把B1和B2分数当作完全等价。\n\n## B. 阅读与信息核实｜15分｜8分钟\n\n阅读以下内部简报，用英文短句回答5个问题，每题3分。阅读材料可一直查看。\n\n> Factory A produced 900 units in Week 1 against a plan of 1,000. Of the 900 units produced, 36 were defective. The defect rate was 3.0% in the previous week. On-time delivery fell from 92% to 88%. A supplier has reported that 200 components will arrive on 18 November instead of 16 November. The impact on the customer delivery date has not been confirmed. Alex from Procurement will confirm the earliest available delivery date by 14:00 China Standard Time (UTC+8) on 13 November. Mei from Production Planning will assess whether the current inventory can cover production until the components arrive. The team should not confirm a revised customer delivery date before the assessment is complete.\n\n1. What percentage of the production plan was completed?\n2. What was the defect rate in Week 1, and by how many percentage points did it change?\n3. By how many percentage points did on-time delivery change?\n4. Who must confirm the earliest available component delivery date, and by when?\n5. Can the team already confirm that the customer delivery will be delayed by two days? Explain.\n\n## C. 邮件写作｜25分｜18分钟\n\n沿用上面的情境。你是项目支持成员，要给采购同事Alex写一封英文邮件，抄送项目经理。\n\n任务：写120—160词，包含主题和称呼。说明已知的物料日期变化及数量；请求Alex按简报给定期限确认最早交付日期；请其说明分批交付是否可行；说明生产计划同事将核查库存；区分已经确认的信息和仍在评估的客户影响；安排下一次更新。\n\n可自定下一次更新的合理时间，但请把它写为你的沟通安排，不要凭空替供应商承诺交货。你不拥有批准替代料、批准加急费用或承诺客户交期的权限。\n\n完成后记录：实际用时、词数、自认为最弱的两句。不提前参考03中的示范。\n\n## D. 口头表达｜25分｜12分钟\n\n用2分钟准备，只能写英文关键词；录音后不重录首测版本。剩余时间用于保存文件和记录。\n\n### D1：求职自我介绍｜60—90秒\n\n> Please introduce yourself and explain why your statistics background is relevant to a project management or data analyst role in manufacturing.\n\n至少说清：教育背景、目标岗位、一项真实做过的任务、你的个人贡献、希望创造的业务价值。未确认的业绩数字不用。允许选择一个岗位作为主要方向。\n\n### D2：数据与项目更新｜90—120秒\n\n使用B部分简报向经理汇报：结论、两个关键数字、目前的风险、尚未确认的事情、下一步行动和需要的支持。不要逐句翻译原文。\n\n额外提醒：36/900=本周缺陷率；客户交期变化不等于供应商到货变化。\n\n## E. 即时互动｜15分｜10分钟\n\n准备30秒，之后由伙伴或AI担当同事，连续提出3个情境问题，每题约20—40秒回答，并做一次追问。评估者从03文件题库选择，不提前逐题背诵。\n\n必须包含：一次信息澄清、一次礼貌异议或风险解释、一次明确下一步/责任人/时间的确认。语音方式优先。\n\n## 交卷模板\n\n姓名/日期：\n\n听力材料、级别、播放次数：\n\n听力答对题数C/总题数N、得分：\n\n阅读1—5：\n\n邮件原稿、用时、词数：\n\nD1/D2录音位置、时长（如暂时只有文字，请明确标注）：\n\n互动方式、题目、记录：\n\n是否使用查词/翻译/改写：\n\n最想优先解决的问题：\n\n## W4、W8、W12复测\n\n保持60分钟、相同五项权重和评分标准。由评估者临时替换工厂、时间、数量、责任人和风险，不把下面的情境直接扩写成可背诵答案。\n\n| 节点 | 听力材料（提前保留，不作日常练习） | 阅读、邮件与口语换题方向 |\n|---|---|---|\n| W4 | [A business interview，B2](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b2/business-interview) | 样件延期，研发/测试资源冲突，请求澄清并发送行动纪要 |\n| W8 | B2 Listening目录中的Business news | 质量指标异常，样本与时间窗口不同，数据请求和分析说明 |\n| W12 | B2 Listening目录中的A lecture about an experiment | 供应短缺+质量变化，提出方案、处理质疑、更新项目经理 |\n\n[B2 Listening目录](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b2)。起点用B1者，在B1目录挑选未学过的同级材料；达到升级条件后再转B2并单独记录。不同音频/题目难度不完全等同，分数变化结合用时、遗漏和沟通闭环判断。\n\nW4前不练A business interview；W8前不练Business news；W12前不练A lecture about an experiment。若已经学过，评估者另选陌生材料并记下变更。C1的A project management meeting可作后续挑战材料，不作为起点必测任务。\n","# 评分、订正与复测出题指南\n\n请在02文件独立完成后阅读。分数只用于本路线的学习决策，不是正式语言等级评定。\n\n## 1. 阅读参考答案｜15分\n\n每题3分，接受意思一致的英文表述。阅读题侧重理解，少量不影响含义的语法错误不另扣。\n\n1. 90%: 900 divided by 1,000. 正确百分比3分；只写900/1000未完成计算1分。\n2. 4.0%, up 1.0 percentage point from 3.0%. 本周缺陷率正确1分；变化数值正确1分；明确percentage point且方向正确1分。若补充相对增幅，约33.3%，不是增加1%。\n3. It fell by 4 percentage points, from 92% to 88%. 方向1分、数值1分、百分点单位1分。相对降幅约4.35%，但本题问百分点。\n4. Alex from Procurement, by 14:00 China Standard Time (UTC+8) on 13 November. 责任人1分、日期1分、时间及明确时区1分。\n5. No. The components are expected two days later, but the impact on customer delivery is still being assessed. Inventory coverage may affect that impact. 否定已确认客户延期1分；区分物料日期和客户日期1分；说明评估/库存因素1分。\n\n## 2. 邮件评分｜25分\n\n每个维度0—5分，五个维度相加。\n\n| 维度 | 5分时的表现 |\n|---|---|\n| 事实准确 | 200件、16→18 November、确认期限准确；没有编造根因或保证客户交期 |\n| 请求可执行 | 请求最早交期、分批可行性、回复期限；收件人知道要做什么 |\n| 结构清楚 | 主题具体，目的先行，段落清楚，行动容易找到 |\n| 语气与协作 | 礼貌直接；说明库存评估与下次更新；没有越权指令 |\n| 语言与可读性 | 用词、时态、介词和标点足以支持理解；句子简明 |\n\n统一档位：5=独立完整且清楚；4=基本完整、只有一个小缺口；3=完成主要目的、仍需少量澄清；2=遗漏关键点或多处歧义，需要明显修改；1=只有零散可用信息；0=未完成/偏离任务。对包含多个要点的维度，按整体完成度评分并列出扣分证据。\n\n写错数量、日期、指标，或把未确认信息说成承诺，事实维度最高2分并标注具体错误；不额外重复扣总分。字数稍有偏离不机械扣分，若冗长或太短造成信息缺失，计入相应维度。测试超过18分钟时保留截止时的版本计分，后续编辑作为练习稿。\n\n### 可参考的邮件（完成测试后再看）\n\nSubject: Delivery update needed: 200 components\n\nHi Alex,\n\nThe supplier has reported that 200 components will arrive on 18 November rather than 16 November. We are assessing the impact on the production plan and customer delivery.\n\nCould you please confirm the earliest available delivery date by 14:00 China Standard Time (UTC+8) on 13 November? Please also check whether a partial shipment is possible and, if so, confirm the quantity and timing.\n\nMei will check whether current inventory can cover production until the components arrive. The impact on the customer delivery date has not yet been confirmed, so we need to complete this assessment before communicating a revised date.\n\nI will consolidate the procurement and planning updates and send the project manager a status update by 16:00 China Standard Time on 13 November.\n\nThanks for your support.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n这只是表达示例。实际工作中的更新期限应先确认输入可得性；自定的16:00为模拟练习安排。\n\n## 3. 口头表达评分｜25分\n\nD1与D2共同评分，各维度0—5，使用邮件部分的统一档位，并补充以下观察点。\n\n| 维度 | 满分表现 |\n|---|---|\n| 任务与事实 | 自我介绍有真实个人贡献；更新准确，区分事实、风险和未决事项 |\n| 结构与重点 | 先讲主要结论；数字支持结论；最后提出行动或请求 |\n| 语言组织 | 能用自己的句子表达，语法和词汇错误不妨碍理解 |\n| 流畅与自主 | 不读全文，能连续表达；停顿不妨碍完成任务，能自我修复 |\n| 发音与可懂度 | 数字、日期、关键词可辨；整体听者能理解；不以母语口音为扣分依据 |\n\n只收到文字稿时：最多反馈前3项，总计15分；后2项写“未测”，不按比例补齐成25分。即使文字看起来流利，也不能据此判断真实口语流畅度或发音。\n\n记录辅助指标：任务是否按时完成；超过3秒的停顿次数；影响理解的数字错误；依靠中文提示的次数。这些帮助比较进步，不单独作为机械扣分表。\n\n### D2内容参考（不要求背诵）\n\nProduction reached 900 units against a plan of 1,000, so we achieved 90% of the plan. The defect rate rose from 3% to 4%, an increase of one percentage point. On-time delivery also fell by four percentage points to 88%. We should not assume that the supplier delay caused these changes; the brief does not establish that link. The 200 components are now expected on 18 November. Alex will confirm the earliest available delivery date, while Mei checks inventory coverage. The impact on customer delivery is still under review.\n\n## 4. 互动评分｜15分\n\n三个维度各0—5分：理解并回应问题；主动澄清/确认；推动下一步且语气得当。接受合理的复述请求，不因听不清时主动澄清而扣分；若重复解释后仍未理解，记录理解问题。\n\n语音互动需要真实来回交流。预先写好的三段答案不算完整互动。文本互动只标“文本条件下X/15”，不要并入语音初测总分。\n\n### 评估者题库（每次选3题并追问）\n\n1. 同事说：Please send the report by Friday. 观察考生是否核实具体日期、时间/时区、报告范围或版本；追问：I need it for a management review.\n2. 经理说：The defect rate went from 3% to 4%, so it only increased by one percent, right? 观察能否礼貌纠正百分点与相对变化；追问：How would you explain that to a non-technical audience?\n3. 采购说：The supplier says the parts should arrive soon. 观察是否追问日期、数量、确认程度；追问：I haven't received written confirmation yet.\n4. 经理说：Can we promise the customer that delivery will remain on schedule? 观察是否说明库存评估未完成、给出确认路径；追问：When can I get an update?\n5. 业务方说：Your dashboard doesn't match my spreadsheet. 观察是否先核对指标定义、筛选条件、刷新时间和粒度；追问：My file only includes completed orders.\n6. 项目同事说：I can't finish both tasks this week. 观察是否核对优先级、依赖、工作量并请求决策；追问：Both owners say their task is urgent.\n\n## 5. 复测出题卡\n\n评估者在当次测试开始时才给新题。沿用02的时限、题型、评分标准，控制阅读长度约90—130词、5个信息问题、邮件120—160词、口头两题、互动三轮。\n\n### W4：样件与测试\n\n模拟参数：计划200件样件，完成180件，其中9件需返工；上一批返工率4%；测试台周三可用但关键样件周四才到；客户验证时间是否变动未确认。指定采购责任人、具体回复时点、测试负责人。要求计算完成率90%、返工率5%、增加1个百分点；解释资源冲突；写协调与升级邮件。不要把返工率和缺陷率混为一个指标。\n\n### W8：数据口径差异\n\n模拟参数：报表A含1000张已完成订单，其中900张按时；报表B含1200张全部订单，其中仍是这900张被标记为按时完成；原始时间窗口和取消订单处理待确认。要求分别说明90%和75%，指出分母不一致，不直接认定绩效下降；给数据负责人写口径核实邮件。补充同口径上一周按时率92%，本周90%，下降2个百分点。\n\n### W12：综合风险\n\n模拟参数：计划1500件、产出1350件、缺陷27件；前期缺陷率2.5%；300件物料预计晚3天，库存是否覆盖仍待核实；两个方案涉及加急成本和排产变更且尚未批准。要求计算完成率90%、缺陷率2%、下降0.5个百分点；不给供应延迟和质量变化强加因果；做风险更新、提出审批请求并写跟进邮件。\n\n每次替换人物、日期、数字时重新算答案，确保单位和分母一致。上面的参数已公开给考生，所以正式复测应换数值并增加一个新的追问，不直接使用原卡作为陌生题。跨次分数仅作趋势参考，不视为经过等值化的标准测验。\n\n## 6. 反馈格式\n\n1. 列出分项得分、未测项目、原句/答案作为证据。\n2. 标出最影响业务理解的3处问题，优先处理数字、承诺边界、行动不明确。\n3. 给一个保留原意、符合当前水平的改法，并说明原因。\n4. 让考生自己重写/重说。\n5. 换人物、日期或业务约束，再做一次迁移练习。\n\n只有所有项目按约定完成才报告完整100分；否则报告已测分/对应满分，并明确缺少什么。\n","# 日常练习包｜同一材料，听说写测\n\n每天90分钟，围绕当天所在章节练习。邮件任务、事实清单和范文与该周听力对应；完整内容见《听力与邮件联动练习》。\n\n## 每天的练习顺序\n\n- 15分钟听力：不看原文听一遍，写下人物、数字、状态、责任人与期限，再看原文核对。\n- 10分钟跟读：选2—3句逐句播放、暂停复述、录音回听，重点检查数字与重音。\n- 25分钟表达：阅读本章根据简历整理的标准回答，列4个关键词，再脱稿说。用自己的职责、动作和交付物回应追问。\n- 25分钟写作：在工作台播放同周听力，依据事实清单写首稿，再对照同材料邮件范文修改。\n- 15分钟复用与记录：用5个本章词汇造句，记录3个关键问题和实际学习分钟。\n\n每周末完成章节综合检测：25道词汇题＋2道同周听力情境题，20分钟。统一提交与解析，错词进入复习。起点、W4、W8、W12另做听读写说阶段测评。\n\n## 四个可反复使用的框架\n\n### 项目更新：Status → Risk → Impact → Action → Request\n\n先说明已知状态，再说明风险、影响确认程度、行动责任人与需要的支持。\n\n### 数据说明：Finding → Evidence → Interpretation → Next step\n\n写清分母、基准与变化，区分百分比和百分点；原因没有查清时说明下一步核查。\n\n### 邮件：Purpose → Context → Request → Timing → Follow-up\n\n录音给出期限时保留日期、时间和时区；没有给出时，不把自行拟定的时点写成已约定期限。\n\n### 面试经历：Context → Task → Your action → Deliverable → Learning\n\n各章已提供完整个人回答。先理解自己做了什么，再练简短表达；支持工作准确说明为支持。\n\n## 同周事实核对\n\n- W3：部件预计晚两天，客户交付影响未确认；Alex 明天14:00中国标准时间确认最早交期。\n- W4：200件部件晚两天；询问最早交期与分批可行性；11月13日14:00中国标准时间前回复。\n- W5：计划1000、产出900、缺陷36、缺陷率4%、上期3%；增加1个百分点，相对约33%。录音没有交付及时率。\n- W7：分批80件，剩余120件日期未确认；加急需要报价与批准。\n- W8：采购查分批排程、计划查库存；加急决定未决；按约定时间更新，录音没有具体时点。\n- W12：产量低于计划但缺陷率改善；供应问题与质量变化的联系尚未建立。\n\n其他章节以工作台对应录音和事实清单为准。\n\n## 陪练与复盘\n\n工作台的“复制陪练提示词”自动带入本章任务、完整听力原文、事实清单和简历参考回答。陪练围绕同一材料，一次提一个问题，结束后指出三个关键问题，再重写或重说。\n\n首稿和修改稿分别标注，保留在草稿框中。录音主动下载；学习档案可导出草稿、日志、词汇状态和测验记录的JSON备份。记录仍保存在当前浏览器。\n","# 听力与邮件联动练习｜12周标准回答\n\n每周顺序：听本周录音 → 记事实 → 写对应邮件 → 对照范文修改 → 完成27题章节综合检测（25词汇＋2情境，20分钟）。\n\n口头回答根据个人经历整理；邮件沿用本周录音的模拟情境。原始简历、联系方式和内部业务文件不作为网站附件。\n\n## W1｜把自己介绍清楚\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nMy academic background is in statistics, and I am interested in project management and data analysis in manufacturing. During my internship at AUMOVIO, I supported project tracking by keeping owners, planned dates, status updates and open risks organised. In a data operations internship, I used Python to combine order and user journey data from different platforms and prepare consistent summaries. These experiences taught me that useful analysis starts with clear definitions and ends with a clear next action. I would like to bring my analytical skills and coordination experience to a team where I can help people understand the situation and make informed decisions.\n\n我的专业背景是统计学，希望从事制造业项目管理或数据分析。在 AUMOVIO 实习时，我整理责任人、计划日期、状态更新和未解决风险，支持项目跟踪。在数据运营实习中，我使用 Python 整合不同平台的订单与用户链路数据，形成口径一致的汇总。这些经历让我认识到，有用的分析始于清晰定义，也要落实到明确的下一步。我希望将分析与协调经验用于帮助团队理解现状并作出有依据的决策。\n\n经历依据：统计学背景；AUMOVIO 项目跟踪；适趣 AI 多平台运营数据整理。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nMy academic background is in statistics, and I am interested in project management and data analysis in manufacturing.\n\nI enjoy turning complex information into a clear summary that helps a team decide what to do next.\n\nFor example, I would explain the data source, check the definitions, and make the key findings easy to understand.\n\nI would also confirm the action owner and the next update, so that the analysis leads to a useful decision.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n听完 W1《自我介绍》后，写80—110词的同事介绍邮件。围绕录音中的统计学背景、制造业 PM / DA 兴趣、数据来源和口径核查、责任人与下一次更新，不额外添加录音未提到的成果数字。\n\n- 背景：statistics；方向：manufacturing project management / data analysis\n- 方法：说明数据来源、核查定义、清楚展示关键发现\n- 闭环：确认 action owner 和 next update\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Introduction and how I can support the team\n\nHi team,\n\nMy academic background is in statistics, and I am interested in project management and data analysis in manufacturing. I enjoy turning complex information into a clear summary that helps a team decide what to do next. When working on an analysis, I would explain the data source, check the definitions and make the key findings easy to understand. I would also confirm the action owner and the next update so that the analysis supports a useful decision. I look forward to working with you.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W2｜让经历经得起追问\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nOne example is my work on multi-platform operations data. The information came from different order and user journey tables, so the same business status could be recorded in different ways. My task was to prepare a consistent basis for reporting. I used Python and pandas to map fields, match records across tables and group the results by business dimensions. I also organised the definitions for order verification, group joining and refunds. The deliverables were reusable processing scripts and reporting outputs. My contribution was the data preparation and definition work. If I repeated the task, I would confirm the status definitions with the users earlier, before building the reporting logic.\n\n一个例子是我整理多平台运营数据的工作。订单和用户链路分散在不同表中，同一种业务状态可能有不同记录方式。我的任务是为报表准备一致的数据基础。我使用 Python 和 pandas 做字段映射、跨表匹配与按业务维度汇总，并整理核销、加群、退款等状态定义，交付可复用的处理脚本和报表输出。我的具体贡献是数据准备和口径整理。如果再做一次，我会在编写报表逻辑之前更早与使用者确认定义。\n\n经历依据：适趣 AI：跨平台字段映射、状态口径统一、分组汇总与可复用报表流程。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nLet me use a fictional project example to explain how I would structure an interview answer.\n\nThe team needed a reliable weekly report, but different colleagues were using different status definitions.\n\nMy role in this example was to compare the source records, clarify the definitions, and prepare a consistent summary.\n\nThe result was a report that showed the open questions, the responsible people, and the next actions.\n\nIn a real interview, I would replace this example with my own experience and include only results I could explain.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n听完 W2《面试追问》后，写90—120词的练习复盘邮件，概述录音中的虚构周报案例：状态定义不一致、比对源记录、澄清定义、汇总未决问题/责任人/行动。明确这只是练习案例。\n\n- 这是 fictional project example，不能写成真实任职成果\n- 问题：同一状态使用不同定义\n- 动作：比对源记录、澄清定义、一致汇总；产出：未决问题、责任人与行动\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Practice recap: building a consistent weekly report\n\nHi coach,\n\nHere is my recap of the fictional project example in this week’s recording. The team needed a reliable weekly report, but colleagues were using different definitions for the same status. The role in the example was to compare source records, clarify the definitions and prepare a consistent summary. The resulting report showed the open questions, the responsible people and the next actions. The example helped me structure an answer around the challenge, my role, my actions and the deliverable. In an actual interview, I would use my own experience and only describe results I can explain.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W3｜做一次有行动的项目周报\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nAt AUMOVIO, I supported project coordination by maintaining a cross-functional tracking list. I kept the responsible person, planned date, current status and open risk together so that updates could be reviewed consistently. When preparing a status update, I focused on what had changed, what was still open and who needed to provide the next confirmation. My role was to maintain and follow up on the information used for coordination. This experience taught me to separate a confirmed delay from a possible downstream impact, and to close an update with an owner and a clear next step.\n\n在 AUMOVIO，我通过维护跨职能跟踪表支持项目协调，将责任人、计划日期、当前状态和未解决风险放在一起，便于一致地审阅更新。准备状态汇报时，我关注哪些事项发生变化、哪些仍未解决，以及下一步需要谁确认。我的职责是维护并跟进协调所需的信息。这段经历让我学会区分已确认延期与可能的后续影响，并在更新结束时说明责任人与下一步。\n\n经历依据：AUMOVIO：维护跨职能项目 Tracking，整理责任人、计划日期、状态与风险。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nHere is a short update on the sample build. We have completed the assembly plan, but the validation milestone is at risk.\n\nA required component is now expected two days later than planned.\n\nProduction Planning is checking inventory coverage, so the impact on customer delivery is not yet confirmed.\n\nAlex will confirm the earliest available delivery date by two p.m. China Standard Time tomorrow.\n\nWe need support from the project manager to resolve the testing resource conflict before the next review.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W3《项目周报》写100—140词状态邮件：装配计划已完成；验证节点有风险；关键部件预计晚两天；库存覆盖在核查，客户交付影响未确认；Alex 明天14:00中国标准时间确认最早交期；请求经理协调测试资源。\n\n- assembly plan 已完成；validation milestone at risk\n- 部件预计延迟两天；Production Planning 正在核查库存覆盖\n- 客户交付影响未确认；Alex 明天14:00 China Standard Time 回报最早交期\n- 经理需在下次评审前协调 testing resource conflict\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Sample build update: validation risk and next actions\n\nHi team,\n\nWe have completed the assembly plan for the sample build, but the validation milestone is at risk. A required component is now expected two days later than planned. Production Planning is checking inventory coverage, so the impact on customer delivery is not yet confirmed.\n\nAlex will confirm the earliest available delivery date by 14:00 China Standard Time tomorrow. We need support from the project manager to resolve the testing resource conflict before the next review. Once the delivery date and inventory coverage are confirmed, we can assess the implications for the build. I will keep the confirmed facts and open items separate in the status update.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W4｜写清一封邮件，跟完一件事\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nIn a business operations internship, I worked with historical price adjustment emails. My task was to turn information spread across messages into structured records. I organised the customer, product or route, price type, effective date and source for each record. Keeping the source was important because a reviewer might need to return to the original message and confirm the context. This experience strengthened my attention to dates, definitions and traceability. When I write a work email, I use the same approach: state the purpose, make the requested information specific and explain how the response will be used.\n\n在业务运营实习中，我整理过历史调价邮件，将分散在邮件里的信息变成结构化记录，统一客户、产品或线路、价格类型、生效时间与来源。保留来源方便复核者回到原邮件确认上下文。这段经历加强了我对日期、定义和可追溯性的关注。写工作邮件时，我也采用同样的思路：说明目的、明确需要的信息，并解释回复将用于什么工作。\n\n经历依据：一知智能：将调价邮件整理成包含客户、价格类型、生效时间与来源的结构化记录。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nHi Alex. I am writing to follow up on the delivery of two hundred components.\n\nThe supplier has reported a two day delay, and we are assessing the effect on the production plan.\n\nCould you please confirm the earliest available delivery date and whether a partial shipment is possible?\n\nPlease send your update by two p.m. China Standard Time on the thirteenth of November.\n\nI will combine your update with the inventory assessment and send the project manager a summary. Thank you for your support.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W4《邮件沟通》写100—140词给 Alex 的邮件：200件部件延迟两天；请求确认最早交期及能否分批；11月13日14:00中国标准时间前回复；将其回复与库存评估合并后向项目经理汇报。\n\n- 收件人 Alex；200 components；供应商报告延迟两天\n- 确认 earliest available delivery date 和 partial shipment 可行性\n- 回复期限：13 November，14:00 China Standard Time\n- 合并交期更新与 inventory assessment 后发给项目经理\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Confirmation needed: delivery of 200 components\n\nHi Alex,\n\nI am writing to follow up on the delivery of 200 components. The supplier has reported a two-day delay, and we are assessing the effect on the production plan. Could you please confirm the earliest available delivery date and whether a partial shipment is possible?\n\nPlease send your update by 14:00 China Standard Time on 13 November. I will combine your update with the inventory assessment and send the project manager a summary. Your confirmation will help us assess the available delivery options using the latest information. If either point is still uncertain, please identify it clearly in your reply. Thank you for your support.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W5｜把数字讲成业务结论\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nIn a data operations internship, I prepared summaries of order and user journey metrics across platforms. I grouped the data by dimensions such as date, platform and product, and produced trend outputs for review. When a metric moved, I used the historical patterns and related indicators to identify items that needed a closer look. My task was to provide a consistent data basis and a clear review direction. I would explain a finding by stating the metric definition, the comparison period and the observed change, then describe the checks needed before drawing a conclusion about the cause.\n\n在数据运营实习中，我汇总过跨平台的订单与用户链路指标，按日期、平台、商品等维度分组并输出趋势，供业务复核。出现变化时，我结合历史模式及相关指标，筛出需要进一步查看的项目。我的任务是提供一致的数据基础和清晰的复核方向。汇报发现时，我会先说明指标定义、比较区间和观测变化，再说明判断原因之前需要做哪些检查。\n\n经历依据：适趣 AI：按日期、平台、商品等维度汇总指标并输出趋势，形成波动复核线索。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nWe produced nine hundred units against a plan of one thousand, so we achieved ninety percent of the production plan.\n\nOf the nine hundred units produced, thirty six were defective. The defect rate was therefore four percent.\n\nThe previous rate was three percent, so the increase was one percentage point, or about thirty three percent in relative terms.\n\nWe should check product mix and reporting consistency before drawing conclusions about the cause.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W5《数据汇报》写100—130词分析邮件，只使用录音数字：计划1000、产出900、缺陷36、缺陷率4%、上期3%、增加1个百分点/相对约33%。提出检查产品组合与报表一致性，不加入录音未出现的交付及时率。\n\n- 计划1000；产出900；计划完成率90%\n- 36 / 900 = 4%；上期3%\n- 上升1 percentage point；相对上升约33%\n- 下一步：check product mix and reporting consistency；原因未确定\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Production summary: output and defect rate\n\nHi manager,\n\nWe produced 900 units against a plan of 1,000, achieving 90% of the production plan. Of the 900 units produced, 36 were defective, so the defect rate was 4%. The previous rate was 3%. This means the rate increased by one percentage point, or about 33% in relative terms.\n\nThe output was below plan and the defect rate was higher than the previous rate. These figures describe the change, but they do not establish its cause. Before drawing a conclusion, we should check product mix and reporting consistency. Those checks will help us decide what further analysis is needed.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W6｜先对齐口径，再解释差异\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nIn a business operations internship, I compared Excel records with BI outputs used for monthly performance calculations. The challenge was that differences could come from several sources, including billed quantities, price versions and missing fields. I organised the differences and reviewed the data collection process rather than assuming one report was automatically correct. The output was a difference analysis and suggestions for improving the extraction process. This experience taught me to align definitions before explaining a gap, and to retain enough detail for another person to trace the difference back to its source.\n\n在业务运营实习中，我对比过用于月度绩效核算的 Excel 记录与 BI 输出。差异可能来自计费数量、价格版本和字段缺失等多种原因。我整理差异并复核取数流程，而不是直接认定某一份报表正确，最终形成差异分析与取数流程改进建议。这让我学会先对齐定义再解释差异，并保留足够明细，方便他人追溯到源头。\n\n经历依据：一知智能：Excel 与 BI 核对；从计费数量、价格版本、字段缺失等方向排查差异。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nBefore comparing the two dashboards, could we confirm the metric definitions?\n\nDoes your spreadsheet include only completed orders, or does it include all orders?\n\nAre both reports using the same reporting period, time zone, and level of detail?\n\nWe should also check duplicate records and the time of the last data refresh.\n\nOnce those conditions are aligned, we can investigate any remaining difference and agree on the next action.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W6《核实口径》写100—140词澄清邮件，逐项询问：完成订单还是全部订单、统计区间、时区、粒度、重复记录、最后刷新时间。录音没有约定回复期限，不自行填写成已约定日期。\n\n- 先确认 metric definitions\n- completed orders 还是 all orders\n- reporting period、time zone、level of detail 是否一致\n- 检查 duplicate records、last data refresh；对齐后再解释剩余差异\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Clarification needed: dashboard and spreadsheet definitions\n\nHi colleague,\n\nBefore comparing the two dashboards, could we confirm the metric definitions? Does your spreadsheet include only completed orders, or does it include all orders? Are both reports using the same reporting period, time zone and level of detail?\n\nWe should also check duplicate records and the time of the last data refresh. These points may affect whether the figures are directly comparable. Once the definitions and reporting conditions are aligned, we can identify any remaining difference and explain it more clearly. Please share the relevant definitions and refresh information so that we can review the comparison on a consistent basis.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W7｜处理供应与验证的冲突\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nAt AUMOVIO, I worked on material risk tracking by organising material status, relevant dates and responsible contacts in a tracking record. The purpose was to give the team a consistent basis for follow-up and escalation. My responsibility was to keep the information structured and make open items visible. This experience showed me why supply discussions need clear ownership and current information. When reviewing options, I would distinguish a supplier indication from a confirmed commitment, list the missing information and identify which team needs to confirm it before a decision is made.\n\n在 AUMOVIO，我将物料状态、相关日期和责任接口整理进跟踪记录，支持物料风险跟踪，为团队跟进和升级提供一致依据。我的职责是保持信息结构清晰并呈现未解决事项。这让我理解供应讨论为什么需要明确责任与最新信息。比较方案时，我会区分供应商意向与已确认承诺，列出缺失信息，并明确决策前需要哪个团队确认。\n\n经历依据：AUMOVIO：物料状态与断点台账，归集时间节点及责任接口，支持风险跟踪。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nThe supplier can offer a partial shipment of eighty units, but the date for the remaining one hundred and twenty is not confirmed.\n\nOne option is to use current inventory for the initial build. Another option is to request expedited shipping.\n\nExpedited shipping would require a quotation and approval, so we should not treat it as a confirmed plan.\n\nCould Production Planning confirm inventory coverage while Procurement checks the supplier schedule?\n\nAfter those updates, the project manager can review the options and make the required decision.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W7《供应与验证》写110—150词风险邮件：供应商可分批80件，余下120件日期未确认；方案为现有库存支持首批或申请加急；加急需要报价和批准；计划查库存、采购查供应商排程，再由经理评审。\n\n- 可分批80件；剩余120件日期未确认\n- 方案一：current inventory 支持 initial build；方案二：expedited shipping\n- 加急需要 quotation and approval，不能写成已批准\n- Production Planning 核查库存；Procurement 核查供应商排程；经理再审议\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Supply risk: partial shipment and delivery options\n\nHi manager,\n\nThe supplier can offer a partial shipment of 80 units, but the date for the remaining 120 units is not confirmed. We have two options to review: use current inventory for the initial build, or request expedited shipping.\n\nThe inventory option depends on available coverage. Expedited shipping would require a quotation and approval, so it should not be treated as a confirmed plan. Could Production Planning confirm inventory coverage while Procurement checks the supplier schedule? After those updates, you can review the options and make the required decision. The date for the remaining units and the approval for any expedited shipment remain open at this stage.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W8｜从讨论到书面闭环\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nMy project coordination experience taught me to turn a discussion into a clear tracking record. At AUMOVIO, I maintained information on action owners, planned dates, status and risks for cross-functional follow-up. For me, a useful meeting summary should make it easy to see what has been agreed, what remains open and who needs to provide the next update. I would keep a proposed option separate from an approved decision. I would also ask the team to correct any missing owner or date, so that the written record supports the next round of follow-up.\n\n项目协调经历让我学会将讨论转化为清晰的跟踪记录。在 AUMOVIO，我维护行动责任人、计划时间、状态和风险，支持跨职能跟进。我认为有用的会议总结应当让人清楚看到已达成什么、仍有什么未解决，以及下一次由谁更新。我会将提议与已批准决定分开，也会请团队补正缺失的责任人或日期，让书面记录支持后续跟进。\n\n经历依据：AUMOVIO：跨职能 Tracking 与责任人/状态/计划时间维护。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nBefore we finish, let me summarise what we have agreed.\n\nProcurement will confirm the partial shipment schedule, and Production Planning will check inventory coverage.\n\nThe decision on expedited shipping remains open until we receive the quotation.\n\nI will update the action list and send the next status by the agreed time.\n\nPlease let me know if I have missed anything, or if an action owner or due date needs to be corrected.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W8《会议闭环》写90—130词会后邮件：采购确认分批排程；计划查库存覆盖；加急决定在报价前保持未决；更新行动表并按约定时间发状态。录音没有具体日期，用 agreed time，不编造时点。\n\n- Procurement：确认 partial shipment schedule\n- Production Planning：检查 inventory coverage\n- expedited shipping decision：报价收到前仍为 open\n- 更新 action list，按 agreed time 发送下一次状态；请团队纠正遗漏的责任人/日期\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Meeting follow-up: supply actions and open decision\n\nHi team,\n\nThank you for the discussion. We agreed that Procurement will confirm the partial shipment schedule, while Production Planning will check inventory coverage. The decision on expedited shipping remains open until we receive the quotation.\n\nI will update the action list and send the next status by the agreed time. The written record will keep the agreed actions separate from the open shipping decision so that we can follow up consistently. Please let me know if I have missed anything, or if an action owner or due date needs to be corrected. I will reflect the corrections in the action list.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W9｜读懂一篇制造业案例\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nMy statistics background has made me careful about how a reported result is defined and measured. In operations analysis, I worked with data from different platforms and prepared consistent metric summaries. That experience is relevant when I read a manufacturing case study. I first identify the business problem and the action taken, then check the baseline, the measurement period and the metric definition. I would attribute a reported outcome to the source and keep it separate from my own interpretation. Before recommending the same approach, I would ask whether the data and operating conditions are comparable.\n\n统计学背景让我关注报告结果如何定义和测量。运营分析中，我处理过不同平台的数据，并整理一致的指标汇总，这种经验也适用于阅读制造业案例。我会先找业务问题和采取的行动，再检查基线、测量期间与指标定义；引用结果时注明来源，并与个人解读分开。在推荐同一方法前，我会追问数据和业务条件是否可比。\n\n经历依据：统计学背景；适趣指标汇总与趋势复核经验。此回答说明分析方法，不宣称个人完成了供应商案例中的成果。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nWhen reading a manufacturing case study, I first identify the business problem and the action taken.\n\nI then check how the reported result was measured, including the time period, the baseline, and the metric definition.\n\nA supplier case study can provide useful context, but its claims should be attributed to the source.\n\nIn my summary, I would separate the reported outcome from my interpretation and mention any important unanswered question.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W9《案例阅读》给同事写90—120词的方法邮件：找问题和行动，核查期间/基线/指标定义，注明供应商来源，区分报告结果与个人解读，列出未解问题。录音没有实际案例成效，不添加改善百分比。\n\n- 步骤：business problem → action taken → measurement\n- 核查 time period、baseline、metric definition\n- supplier claim 要标来源；区分 reported outcome 和 interpretation\n- 录音没有给企业成效数字\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Checks for our manufacturing case study summary\n\nHi colleague,\n\nFor our manufacturing case study summary, I suggest starting with the business problem and the action taken. We should then check how the reported result was measured, including the time period, the baseline and the metric definition.\n\nA supplier case study can provide useful context, but its claims should be attributed to the source. In the summary, we should separate the reported outcome from our interpretation and mention any important unanswered question. The recording does not provide a specific company result, so I would not add an improvement figure. These checks will help us prepare a clear and traceable summary.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W10｜提出建议，也能礼貌异议\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nWhen I discuss a recommendation, I try to connect it to the evidence and the information still needed. In my business operations work, I reviewed differences between Excel and BI outputs and considered possible issues such as quantities, price versions and missing fields. I organised the differences and proposed improvements to the extraction process. In project coordination, I also learned to make responsibilities and open items visible. If a colleague wants to act before the checks are complete, I would acknowledge the objective, explain the remaining uncertainty and propose a practical next step with a clear confirmation owner.\n\n讨论建议时，我会把方案与证据、仍需确认的信息联系起来。业务运营工作中，我核对 Excel 与 BI 的差异，考虑数量、价格版本和字段缺失等可能问题，整理差异并提出取数流程改进建议。项目协调也让我学会呈现责任与未决事项。如果同事想在核查完成前行动，我会先回应目标，再说明尚存不确定性，并提出有明确确认责任人的下一步。\n\n经历依据：一知智能：核算差异分析；AUMOVIO：跨职能信息跟进。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nI see the benefit of bringing the delivery date forward. My concern is that validation would not be complete by then.\n\nCould we keep the original validation window and prioritise the first shipment instead?\n\nThis may help us meet the most urgent need while allowing the team to complete the required checks.\n\nWe would need confirmation from Testing and Production Planning before committing to the revised schedule.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W10《建议与异议》写90—130词邮件：认可提前交付价值，但届时验证未完成；建议保留原验证窗口、优先首批；需 Testing 和 Production Planning 确认后才能承诺调整排程。\n\n- 目标：bring delivery date forward\n- 顾虑：validation would not be complete by then\n- 替代：keep original validation window；prioritise first shipment\n- 需要 Testing 和 Production Planning 确认，再承诺 revised schedule\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Proposal: first shipment priority and validation timing\n\nHi team,\n\nI see the benefit of bringing the delivery date forward. My concern is that validation would not be complete by then. Could we keep the original validation window and prioritise the first shipment instead?\n\nThis may help us meet the most urgent need while allowing the team to complete the required checks. The proposal is intended to balance delivery urgency with the validation work that remains. We would need confirmation from Testing and Production Planning before committing to the revised schedule. Please review whether this approach is feasible so that we can discuss the next step using confirmed information.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W11｜对准你的下一场面试\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nI am interested in this role because it combines structured problem solving with collaboration across teams. My background in statistics helps me work carefully with definitions and evidence. At AUMOVIO, I supported project tracking by organising owners, dates, status updates and risks. In data operations, I used Python to combine records from different platforms and prepare consistent reporting outputs. I also reviewed differences between Excel and BI data in a business operations internship. For a project coordination role, I can bring clear tracking and follow-up. For a data analysis role, I can bring data preparation and reconciliation skills. I would like to understand how success is measured and how this role works with Production, Quality and Procurement.\n\n我对这个岗位感兴趣，因为它结合了结构化解决问题和团队协作。统计学背景帮助我认真处理口径和证据。在 AUMOVIO，我整理责任人、日期、状态和风险，支持项目跟踪；数据运营中，我使用 Python 整合跨平台记录并准备一致的报表输出；业务运营中，我核对过 Excel 与 BI 的差异。项目协调方向我能提供清晰的跟踪与跟进，数据分析方向我能提供数据准备和核对能力。我也希望了解岗位成功标准及其与生产、质量、采购的协作方式。\n\n经历依据：AUMOVIO 项目跟踪；适趣数据处理；一知 Excel/BI 核对。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nA relevant example from my experience should show how I handled information and worked with other people.\n\nI would explain my actual role, the action I took, and the result or deliverable I could verify.\n\nIf I had only supported a process, I would say so clearly and explain which skills could transfer to this position.\n\nI would also ask how success is measured in the role and how the team works with Production, Quality, and Procurement.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W11《岗位面试》的回答原则，给陪练者写90—120词准备邮件：每个例子讲实际职责、个人动作和可核实交付物；支持工作明确说 supported；准备成功标准及生产/质量/采购协作的反问。不要添加录音未提供的面试时间或录用承诺。\n\n- 例子要说明 handled information 和 worked with people\n- 说清 actual role、action、verifiable result / deliverable\n- 支持流程用 supported，说明可迁移能力\n- 反问 success measured 及 Production / Quality / Procurement 协作\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Interview preparation: evidence and role questions\n\nHi coach,\n\nFor my interview preparation, I will choose an example that shows how I handled information and worked with other people. I will explain my actual role, the action I took and a result or deliverable I can verify.\n\nIf I only supported a process, I will describe that scope clearly and explain which skills could transfer to the position. I will also prepare questions about how success is measured in the role and how the team works with Production, Quality and Procurement. Please use these points when reviewing my answer so that the discussion stays focused on evidence and relevance.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n\n## W12｜把英语用进完整工作流\n\n### 简历标准回答\n\nAcross my internships, I have worked on data preparation, reconciliation and project tracking. I used Python to organise multi-platform operations data, reviewed differences between Excel and BI outputs, and maintained project status information with owners and planned dates. The common thread is making information easier to check and act on. In a new manufacturing task, I would first confirm the definitions and sources, then summarise what is known and what remains open. I would explain my finding in plain language, identify the person responsible for the next confirmation and keep a written record for follow-up. That is how I would connect my statistics training with practical team needs.\n\n在几段实习中，我做过数据准备、核对与项目跟踪：使用 Python 整理多平台运营数据，复核 Excel 与 BI 差异，以及维护包含责任人与计划日期的项目状态信息。这些工作的共同点是让信息便于核查并落实到行动。面对新的制造业任务，我会先确认口径与来源，再总结已知和未决事项，用清楚的语言解释发现，明确下一次确认的责任人，并保留书面记录以便跟进。这是我把统计训练与团队实际需求连接起来的方式。\n\n经历依据：统计学背景；适趣数据准备；一知差异核对；AUMOVIO 状态跟踪。\n\n### 同周听力原文\n\nHere is what we know so far. Production is below plan, but the defect rate has improved.\n\nWe have not established a link between the supply issue and the quality change.\n\nThe remaining uncertainty is inventory coverage. Production Planning will confirm it before the next review.\n\nThe project manager can then review the delivery options and any approvals required.\n\nI will record the decision, update the action list, and send a short written summary to the team.\n\n### 邮件任务\n\n根据 W12《完整工作流》写100—140词跟进邮件：产量低于计划但缺陷率改善；尚未建立供应与质量变化之间的联系；库存覆盖未知，由计划在下次评审前确认；项目经理随后审议交付选项及审批；记录决定、更新行动表、书面总结。\n\n- production below plan；defect rate improved；录音无具体数字\n- 未建立 supply issue 与 quality change 的联系\n- 库存覆盖未确认；Production Planning 在 next review 前确认\n- 经理审议 delivery options 和 approvals；记录决定、更新 action list、发总结\n\n### 对应邮件范文\n\nSubject: Follow-up: production status and delivery review\n\nHi team,\n\nHere is what we know so far: production is below plan, but the defect rate has improved. We have not established a link between the supply issue and the quality change. The remaining uncertainty is inventory coverage.\n\nProduction Planning will confirm coverage before the next review. The project manager can then review the delivery options and any approvals required. Until that information is available, the delivery review still has an open input. I will record the decision, update the action list and send a short written summary to the team. This will keep the confirmed status, open question and follow-up actions together.\n\nBest regards,\nLu Kun\n","# 12模块职场英语课程手册\n\n对象：鲁琨；统计学背景；制造业外企项目管理/数据分析。每周一个模块，配合学习路线中的90分钟节奏。\n\n口头表达标准回答根据个人简历与经历核验稿整理。听力及对应邮件为模拟练习，两种情境分别标注。每章综合检测统一包含25道词汇题和2道同周听力情境题；完整词表见词汇手册，听力原文和邮件范文见联动练习手册。\n\n## 第1周｜把自己介绍清楚\n\nStart with your story · 共通\n\n学习目标：能说清背景、目标岗位、个人贡献和业务价值。\n\n重点：不要背整篇稿。先列4个英文关键词，再连成自己的句子。\n\n表达框架：Background → Role → Evidence → Value\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- My academic background is in statistics. — 交代统计学背景。\n- My responsibility was to … — 界定自己真实承担的部分。\n- I would like to apply these skills to … — 把已有能力连接到目标工作。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nMy academic background is in statistics, and I am interested in project management and data analysis in manufacturing. During my internship at AUMOVIO, I supported project tracking by keeping owners, planned dates, status updates and open risks organised. In a data operations internship, I used Python to combine order and user journey data from different platforms and prepare consistent summaries. These experiences taught me that useful analysis starts with clear definitions and ends with a clear next action. I would like to bring my analytical skills and coordination experience to a team where I can help people understand the situation and make informed decisions.\n\n我的专业背景是统计学，希望从事制造业项目管理或数据分析。在 AUMOVIO 实习时，我整理责任人、计划日期、状态更新和未解决风险，支持项目跟踪。在数据运营实习中，我使用 Python 整合不同平台的订单与用户链路数据，形成口径一致的汇总。这些经历让我认识到，有用的分析始于清晰定义，也要落实到明确的下一步。我希望将分析与协调经验用于帮助团队理解现状并作出有依据的决策。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用这份简历标准回答录一段60—90秒自我介绍，再脱稿回答：How did you combine data analysis with project coordination?\n\n写作：听完 W1《自我介绍》后，写80—110词的同事介绍邮件。围绕录音中的统计学背景、制造业 PM / DA 兴趣、数据来源和口径核查、责任人与下一次更新，不额外添加录音未提到的成果数字。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [B1 Speaking](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking/b1)：先学 Meeting face-to-face、Agreeing and disagreeing。看视频后替换成自己的工作场景。\n- [Online English level test](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/english-levels/online-english-level-test)：需免费账号，只作语法词汇粗略定位，不代表口语、听力或工作沟通水平。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W1 听力情境】录音中，分析完成后还应确认什么？\n   A. 责任人与下一次更新\n   B. 未经核实的节省金额\n   C. 所有人已批准方案\n\n2. 【W1 听力情境】哪项符合录音中的工作方式？\n   A. 省略数据来源\n   B. 先检查定义，再清楚展示发现\n   C. 把假设写成已实现成果\n\n参考答案：1. A，录音以 action owner 和 next update 连接分析与行动。；2. B，录音强调说明来源、核查定义并讲清关键发现。\n\n## 第2周｜让经历经得起追问\n\nInterview with evidence · 共通\n\n学习目标：讲清2段真实经历，并连续回答3个追问。\n\n重点：故事中的团队目标和个人动作要分开；先回答问题，再补背景。\n\n表达框架：Context → Task → Your action → Result → Learning\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- The main challenge was … — 先点出具体困难。\n- I checked … before deciding to … — 交代判断依据。\n- One thing I would improve is … — 说明可执行的反思。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nOne example is my work on multi-platform operations data. The information came from different order and user journey tables, so the same business status could be recorded in different ways. My task was to prepare a consistent basis for reporting. I used Python and pandas to map fields, match records across tables and group the results by business dimensions. I also organised the definitions for order verification, group joining and refunds. The deliverables were reusable processing scripts and reporting outputs. My contribution was the data preparation and definition work. If I repeated the task, I would confirm the status definitions with the users earlier, before building the reporting logic.\n\n一个例子是我整理多平台运营数据的工作。订单和用户链路分散在不同表中，同一种业务状态可能有不同记录方式。我的任务是为报表准备一致的数据基础。我使用 Python 和 pandas 做字段映射、跨表匹配与按业务维度汇总，并整理核销、加群、退款等状态定义，交付可复用的处理脚本和报表输出。我的具体贡献是数据准备和口径整理。如果再做一次，我会在编写报表逻辑之前更早与使用者确认定义。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用90秒讲清适趣数据整理经历：困难、个人任务、方法、交付物和一次反思。追问：What was your own contribution?\n\n写作：听完 W2《面试追问》后，写90—120词的练习复盘邮件，概述录音中的虚构周报案例：状态定义不一致、比对源记录、澄清定义、汇总未决问题/责任人/行动。明确这只是练习案例。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [B1 Speaking](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking/b1)：先学 Meeting face-to-face、Agreeing and disagreeing。看视频后替换成自己的工作场景。\n- [Write & Improve](https://writeandimprove.com/)：基础写作练习和自动反馈免费。先独立写首稿，再根据反馈修改；业务事实需另外核查。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W2 听力情境】W2录音中的项目例子属于？\n   A. 已核实的个人成果\n   B. 虚构的回答结构示例\n   C. 客户正式批准记录\n\n2. 【W2 听力情境】示例报告应呈现哪组信息？\n   A. 只有总分\n   B. 没有责任人的问题列表\n   C. 未决问题、责任人与下一步行动\n\n参考答案：1. B，录音明确使用 fictional project example。；2. C，录音中的交付物包含 open questions、responsible people、next actions。\n\n## 第3周｜做一次有行动的项目周报\n\nUpdates that move work forward · 项目管理\n\n学习目标：让听者知道项目在哪里、风险是什么、接下来谁做什么。\n\n重点：on track、at risk、overdue分别表示按计划、有风险、已经逾期。\n\n表达框架：Status → Risk → Impact → Action → Request\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- The milestone is at risk because … — 说明里程碑风险及依据。\n- Alex will confirm the date by … — 写清责任人与时点。\n- We need a decision on … — 把讨论转成具体决策请求。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nAt AUMOVIO, I supported project coordination by maintaining a cross-functional tracking list. I kept the responsible person, planned date, current status and open risk together so that updates could be reviewed consistently. When preparing a status update, I focused on what had changed, what was still open and who needed to provide the next confirmation. My role was to maintain and follow up on the information used for coordination. This experience taught me to separate a confirmed delay from a possible downstream impact, and to close an update with an owner and a clear next step.\n\n在 AUMOVIO，我通过维护跨职能跟踪表支持项目协调，将责任人、计划日期、当前状态和未解决风险放在一起，便于一致地审阅更新。准备状态汇报时，我关注哪些事项发生变化、哪些仍未解决，以及下一步需要谁确认。我的职责是维护并跟进协调所需的信息。这段经历让我学会区分已确认延期与可能的后续影响，并在更新结束时说明责任人与下一步。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：先用简历标准回答说明你如何维护 Tracking，再用 W3 录音中的模拟案例做一次项目更新，明确区分两段情境。\n\n写作：根据 W3《项目周报》写100—140词状态邮件：装配计划已完成；验证节点有风险；关键部件预计晚两天；库存覆盖在核查，客户交付影响未确认；Alex 明天14:00中国标准时间确认最早交期；请求经理协调测试资源。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [B2 Listening](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b2)：先盲听、做题，再看原文。测试保留篇目请在测试中心查看，不提前练。\n- [English for emails](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/business/english-emails)：从 Starting and finishing emails、Making arrangements、Enquiries 开始，每单元后写一封自己的邮件。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W3 听力情境】谁在何时确认最早交期？\n   A. Alex，明天14:00中国标准时间\n   B. 经理，今天下班前\n   C. 采购，下周一\n\n2. 【W3 听力情境】客户交付影响当前是什么状态？\n   A. 确定晚两天\n   B. 尚未确认，库存覆盖仍在核查\n   C. 已经取消交付\n\n参考答案：1. A，W3录音明确给出 Alex、tomorrow 和 two p.m. China Standard Time。；2. B，部件晚两天不等于客户交付已确认延期。\n\n## 第4周｜写清一封邮件，跟完一件事\n\nWrite for a clear next step · 共通\n\n学习目标：在12分钟左右写清事实、请求、期限与下一步。\n\n重点：邮件开头交代目的；收件人应能立即判断要做什么。\n\n表达框架：Purpose → Context → Request → Deadline → Follow-up\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- Could you please confirm … by …? — 提出具体且有期限的请求。\n- The impact is still being assessed. — 标明影响仍在核查。\n- I will send an update by … — 约定下一次沟通。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nIn a business operations internship, I worked with historical price adjustment emails. My task was to turn information spread across messages into structured records. I organised the customer, product or route, price type, effective date and source for each record. Keeping the source was important because a reviewer might need to return to the original message and confirm the context. This experience strengthened my attention to dates, definitions and traceability. When I write a work email, I use the same approach: state the purpose, make the requested information specific and explain how the response will be used.\n\n在业务运营实习中，我整理过历史调价邮件，将分散在邮件里的信息变成结构化记录，统一客户、产品或线路、价格类型、生效时间与来源。保留来源方便复核者回到原邮件确认上下文。这段经历加强了我对日期、定义和可追溯性的关注。写工作邮件时，我也采用同样的思路：说明目的、明确需要的信息，并解释回复将用于什么工作。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用标准回答介绍你如何整理调价邮件，再用 W4 情境口头说明交期确认邮件的两个请求和回复期限。\n\n写作：根据 W4《邮件沟通》写100—140词给 Alex 的邮件：200件部件延迟两天；请求确认最早交期及能否分批；11月13日14:00中国标准时间前回复；将其回复与库存评估合并后向项目经理汇报。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [English for emails](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/business/english-emails)：从 Starting and finishing emails、Making arrangements、Enquiries 开始，每单元后写一封自己的邮件。\n- [Write & Improve](https://writeandimprove.com/)：基础写作练习和自动反馈免费。先独立写首稿，再根据反馈修改；业务事实需另外核查。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W4 听力情境】W4邮件要求 Alex 确认什么？\n   A. 最终质量结论\n   B. 最早交期与分批交付可行性\n   C. 已经批准的加急预算\n\n2. 【W4 听力情境】回复期限应写成？\n   A. Soon\n   B. 13 November，没有时间\n   C. 14:00 China Standard Time on 13 November\n\n参考答案：1. B，录音中有 earliest available delivery date 和 partial shipment 两个请求。；2. C，保留日期、时点与时区，避免含糊的 soon。\n\n## 第5周｜把数字讲成业务结论\n\nFrom numbers to meaning · 数据分析\n\n学习目标：做2分钟数据说明，数字、分母、单位和时间窗口准确。\n\n重点：3%升到4%是上升1个百分点；相对增幅约33.3%。\n\n表达框架：Finding → Evidence → Interpretation → Next step\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- We achieved 90% of the production plan. — 说明计划完成率。\n- The rate rose by one percentage point. — 准确表达百分点变化。\n- The cause has not yet been established. — 区分观察与原因判断。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nIn a data operations internship, I prepared summaries of order and user journey metrics across platforms. I grouped the data by dimensions such as date, platform and product, and produced trend outputs for review. When a metric moved, I used the historical patterns and related indicators to identify items that needed a closer look. My task was to provide a consistent data basis and a clear review direction. I would explain a finding by stating the metric definition, the comparison period and the observed change, then describe the checks needed before drawing a conclusion about the cause.\n\n在数据运营实习中，我汇总过跨平台的订单与用户链路指标，按日期、平台、商品等维度分组并输出趋势，供业务复核。出现变化时，我结合历史模式及相关指标，筛出需要进一步查看的项目。我的任务是提供一致的数据基础和清晰的复核方向。汇报发现时，我会先说明指标定义、比较区间和观测变化，再说明判断原因之前需要做哪些检查。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用标准回答介绍自己的指标汇总经验，再准确复述 W5 的产出完成率、缺陷率、百分点和相对变化。\n\n写作：根据 W5《数据汇报》写100—130词分析邮件，只使用录音数字：计划1000、产出900、缺陷36、缺陷率4%、上期3%、增加1个百分点/相对约33%。提出检查产品组合与报表一致性，不加入录音未出现的交付及时率。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [B2 Listening](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b2)：先盲听、做题，再看原文。测试保留篇目请在测试中心查看，不提前练。\n- [Write & Improve](https://writeandimprove.com/)：基础写作练习和自动反馈免费。先独立写首稿，再根据反馈修改；业务事实需另外核查。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W5 听力情境】W5的缺陷率是多少？\n   A. 36 / 1000 = 3.6%\n   B. 36 / 900 = 4%\n   C. 900 / 1000 = 90%\n\n2. 【W5 听力情境】从3%到4%应如何表述？\n   A. 增加1个百分点，相对约33%\n   B. 增加1%，相对不变\n   C. 增加33个百分点\n\n参考答案：1. B，缺陷率分母为实际产出900，36/900=4%。；2. A，绝对变化4%−3%=1个百分点；相对变化约33%。\n\n## 第6周｜先对齐口径，再解释差异\n\nAsk better data questions · 数据分析\n\n学习目标：能向业务方提出5个有用的核实问题，并写数据请求。\n\n重点：先检查定义、时间、范围和分母，再讨论谁的结果正确。\n\n表达框架：Definition → Scope → Grain → Time → Quality\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- Does this include cancelled orders? — 核查统计范围。\n- What is the denominator for this rate? — 核查分母。\n- When was the dataset last refreshed? — 核查刷新时点。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nIn a business operations internship, I compared Excel records with BI outputs used for monthly performance calculations. The challenge was that differences could come from several sources, including billed quantities, price versions and missing fields. I organised the differences and reviewed the data collection process rather than assuming one report was automatically correct. The output was a difference analysis and suggestions for improving the extraction process. This experience taught me to align definitions before explaining a gap, and to retain enough detail for another person to trace the difference back to its source.\n\n在业务运营实习中，我对比过用于月度绩效核算的 Excel 记录与 BI 输出。差异可能来自计费数量、价格版本和字段缺失等多种原因。我整理差异并复核取数流程，而不是直接认定某一份报表正确，最终形成差异分析与取数流程改进建议。这让我学会先对齐定义再解释差异，并保留足够明细，方便他人追溯到源头。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用标准回答讲一次报表核对经历，再根据 W6 听力提出定义、筛选、时间、粒度、重复记录和刷新时点的问题。\n\n写作：根据 W6《核实口径》写100—140词澄清邮件，逐项询问：完成订单还是全部订单、统计区间、时区、粒度、重复记录、最后刷新时间。录音没有约定回复期限，不自行填写成已约定日期。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [Podcasts for professionals](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/business-english/podcasts-professionals)：第5周起使用 Managing conflict、Change management，抓住观点、理由和行动。\n- [Write & Improve](https://writeandimprove.com/)：基础写作练习和自动反馈免费。先独立写首稿，再根据反馈修改；业务事实需另外核查。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W6 听力情境】比较报表之前首先应做什么？\n   A. 直接认定一张表错误\n   B. 确认指标定义与比较条件\n   C. 把两张表的数字平均\n\n2. 【W6 听力情境】哪项是 W6 要核查的信息？\n   A. 最后刷新时点与重复记录\n   B. 邮件字体大小\n   C. 已经确认的客户投诉金额\n\n参考答案：1. B，W6先核查定义、范围、时间与粒度。；2. A，录音明确要求 check duplicate records 和 last data refresh。\n\n## 第7周｜处理供应与验证的冲突\n\nCoordinate under constraints · 项目管理\n\n学习目标：能说明约束、比较方案、请求批准并确认跟进。\n\n重点：建议、预计、确认和批准是不同状态，要在英语里说清。\n\n表达框架：Constraint → Options → Trade-offs → Approval → Follow-up\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- One option is a partial shipment. — 提出备选方案。\n- This would require approval from … — 说明审批依赖。\n- Could we confirm inventory coverage first? — 先核查关键条件。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nAt AUMOVIO, I worked on material risk tracking by organising material status, relevant dates and responsible contacts in a tracking record. The purpose was to give the team a consistent basis for follow-up and escalation. My responsibility was to keep the information structured and make open items visible. This experience showed me why supply discussions need clear ownership and current information. When reviewing options, I would distinguish a supplier indication from a confirmed commitment, list the missing information and identify which team needs to confirm it before a decision is made.\n\n在 AUMOVIO，我将物料状态、相关日期和责任接口整理进跟踪记录，支持物料风险跟踪，为团队跟进和升级提供一致依据。我的职责是保持信息结构清晰并呈现未解决事项。这让我理解供应讨论为什么需要明确责任与最新信息。比较方案时，我会区分供应商意向与已确认承诺，列出缺失信息，并明确决策前需要哪个团队确认。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用标准回答说明你的物料跟踪职责，再用 W7 模拟情境向经理说明两种方案及其确认条件。\n\n写作：根据 W7《供应与验证》写110—150词风险邮件：供应商可分批80件，余下120件日期未确认；方案为现有库存支持首批或申请加急；加急需要报价和批准；计划查库存、采购查供应商排程，再由经理评审。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [Podcasts for professionals](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/business-english/podcasts-professionals)：第5周起使用 Managing conflict、Change management，抓住观点、理由和行动。\n- [English for emails](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/business/english-emails)：从 Starting and finishing emails、Making arrangements、Enquiries 开始，每单元后写一封自己的邮件。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W7 听力情境】W7供应商当前可提供多少件分批交付？\n   A. 120件，全部已确认\n   B. 80件，剩余120件日期未确认\n   C. 200件全部已到\n\n2. 【W7 听力情境】加急方案目前还需要什么？\n   A. 不需要任何确认\n   B. 报价与批准\n   C. 先宣称客户交付已保证\n\n参考答案：1. B，录音为80件分批方案，剩余120件日期未确认。；2. B，Expedited shipping requires a quotation and approval。\n\n## 第8周｜从讨论到书面闭环\n\nRun a complete work cycle · 共通\n\n学习目标：独立完成一次10分钟讨论和配套书面总结。\n\n重点：决策、建议、待确认事项分开；没有责任人的行动不算完整。\n\n表达框架：Brief → Update → Questions → Decisions → Written follow-up\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- Let me summarise what we have agreed. — 复述已确认的决定。\n- This point remains open. — 标记未决事项。\n- Please let me know if I have missed anything. — 邀请纠正纪要。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nMy project coordination experience taught me to turn a discussion into a clear tracking record. At AUMOVIO, I maintained information on action owners, planned dates, status and risks for cross-functional follow-up. For me, a useful meeting summary should make it easy to see what has been agreed, what remains open and who needs to provide the next update. I would keep a proposed option separate from an approved decision. I would also ask the team to correct any missing owner or date, so that the written record supports the next round of follow-up.\n\n项目协调经历让我学会将讨论转化为清晰的跟踪记录。在 AUMOVIO，我维护行动责任人、计划时间、状态和风险，支持跨职能跟进。我认为有用的会议总结应当让人清楚看到已达成什么、仍有什么未解决，以及下一次由谁更新。我会将提议与已批准决定分开，也会请团队补正缺失的责任人或日期，让书面记录支持后续跟进。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用标准回答讲你如何把会议变成可跟进记录，再用 W8 录音做30秒会议收尾。\n\n写作：根据 W8《会议闭环》写90—130词会后邮件：采购确认分批排程；计划查库存覆盖；加急决定在报价前保持未决；更新行动表并按约定时间发状态。录音没有具体日期，用 agreed time，不编造时点。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [B2 Listening](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b2)：先盲听、做题，再看原文。测试保留篇目请在测试中心查看，不提前练。\n- [English for emails](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/business/english-emails)：从 Starting and finishing emails、Making arrangements、Enquiries 开始，每单元后写一封自己的邮件。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W8 听力情境】W8中哪个决定仍未解决？\n   A. 采购是否负责排程\n   B. 报价收到前的加急决定\n   C. 是否需要行动清单\n\n2. 【W8 听力情境】W8下一次状态应何时发出？\n   A. 按约定时间，录音未给出具体时点\n   B. 明天14:00，所有周通用\n   C. 11月13日，所有周通用\n\n参考答案：1. B，录音说 expedited shipping remains open until we receive the quotation。；2. A，W8只说 by the agreed time，不应借用其他周的时点。\n\n## 第9周｜读懂一篇制造业案例\n\nRead the business behind the words · 共通\n\n学习目标：读250—500词，用90秒复述问题、行动和证据。\n\n重点：案例中的厂商观点、企业自述与独立证据要区分。\n\n表达框架：Problem → Action → Result → Evidence → Question\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- The company aimed to improve … — 说明企业目标。\n- According to the case study, … — 明确归因来源。\n- The article does not explain how … was measured. — 指出尚不明确的测量信息。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nMy statistics background has made me careful about how a reported result is defined and measured. In operations analysis, I worked with data from different platforms and prepared consistent metric summaries. That experience is relevant when I read a manufacturing case study. I first identify the business problem and the action taken, then check the baseline, the measurement period and the metric definition. I would attribute a reported outcome to the source and keep it separate from my own interpretation. Before recommending the same approach, I would ask whether the data and operating conditions are comparable.\n\n统计学背景让我关注报告结果如何定义和测量。运营分析中，我处理过不同平台的数据，并整理一致的指标汇总，这种经验也适用于阅读制造业案例。我会先找业务问题和采取的行动，再检查基线、测量期间与指标定义；引用结果时注明来源，并与个人解读分开。在推荐同一方法前，我会追问数据和业务条件是否可比。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用标准回答说明你的数据经验如何帮助案例评审，再按 W9 录音用英语提出三个证据核查问题。\n\n写作：根据 W9《案例阅读》给同事写90—120词的方法邮件：找问题和行动，核查期间/基线/指标定义，注明供应商来源，区分报告结果与个人解读，列出未解问题。录音没有实际案例成效，不添加改善百分比。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [Manufacturing case studies](https://www.siemens.com/en-us/company/software-case-studies/)：每次只读250—500词，提取 problem / action / result，不必先学会案例中的软件。\n- [NAF：质量管理与透明度](https://resources.sw.siemens.com/en-GB/case-study-naf/)：从 Challenges、Keys to success、Results 开始，用90秒说明业务问题和处理方法。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W9 听力情境】W9核查案例结果时应关注哪组信息？\n   A. 测量期间、基线、指标定义\n   B. 只看标题\n   C. 只看供应商宣传语\n\n2. 【W9 听力情境】录音没有给实际改善数字，应如何写？\n   A. 自行添加一个合理数字\n   B. 注明来源并保留未解问题，不添加数字\n   C. 将供应商说法直接写成独立验证\n\n参考答案：1. A，这三项决定报告结果如何解释和比较。；2. B，保留出处并区分报告结果与自己的解读。\n\n## 第10周｜提出建议，也能礼貌异议\n\nDisagree with a useful alternative · 共通\n\n学习目标：说明顾虑、给出依据和替代方案，并推进决策。\n\n重点：反对意见要连接事实与可执行选择。\n\n表达框架：Acknowledge → Concern → Evidence → Alternative → Decision\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- I see your point. My concern is … — 先回应对方，再提出具体顾虑。\n- Could we consider … instead? — 提出替代方案。\n- What would we need to confirm before deciding? — 推动确认决策条件。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nWhen I discuss a recommendation, I try to connect it to the evidence and the information still needed. In my business operations work, I reviewed differences between Excel and BI outputs and considered possible issues such as quantities, price versions and missing fields. I organised the differences and proposed improvements to the extraction process. In project coordination, I also learned to make responsibilities and open items visible. If a colleague wants to act before the checks are complete, I would acknowledge the objective, explain the remaining uncertainty and propose a practical next step with a clear confirmation owner.\n\n讨论建议时，我会把方案与证据、仍需确认的信息联系起来。业务运营工作中，我核对 Excel 与 BI 的差异，考虑数量、价格版本和字段缺失等可能问题，整理差异并提出取数流程改进建议。项目协调也让我学会呈现责任与未决事项。如果同事想在核查完成前行动，我会先回应目标，再说明尚存不确定性，并提出有明确确认责任人的下一步。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用标准回答说明你如何基于证据提出建议，再按 W10 听力礼貌回应提前交付的要求。\n\n写作：根据 W10《建议与异议》写90—130词邮件：认可提前交付价值，但届时验证未完成；建议保留原验证窗口、优先首批；需 Testing 和 Production Planning 确认后才能承诺调整排程。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [B1 Speaking](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking/b1)：先学 Meeting face-to-face、Agreeing and disagreeing。看视频后替换成自己的工作场景。\n- [Podcasts for professionals](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/business-english/podcasts-professionals)：第5周起使用 Managing conflict、Change management，抓住观点、理由和行动。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W10 听力情境】W10提出的替代方案是什么？\n   A. 跳过验证\n   B. 保留原验证窗口并优先首批\n   C. 立即承诺全部提前交付\n\n2. 【W10 听力情境】调整排程需要谁确认？\n   A. Testing 和 Production Planning\n   B. 任意一个实习生单独批准\n   C. 不需要确认\n\n参考答案：1. B，录音建议 keep the original validation window and prioritise the first shipment。；2. A，录音明确提到这两个团队的确认。\n\n## 第11周｜对准你的下一场面试\n\nPrepare for the actual role · 共通\n\n学习目标：完成20分钟模拟面试和一份限时书面任务。\n\n重点：每个岗位要求对应一条真实证据，未做过的内容说明如何迁移与学习。\n\n表达框架：Requirement → Evidence → Contribution → Transfer\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- A relevant example from my experience is … — 以经历回应岗位要求。\n- I have not owned that process, but I have supported … — 准确说明经验范围。\n- How is success measured in this role? — 询问岗位成功标准。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nI am interested in this role because it combines structured problem solving with collaboration across teams. My background in statistics helps me work carefully with definitions and evidence. At AUMOVIO, I supported project tracking by organising owners, dates, status updates and risks. In data operations, I used Python to combine records from different platforms and prepare consistent reporting outputs. I also reviewed differences between Excel and BI data in a business operations internship. For a project coordination role, I can bring clear tracking and follow-up. For a data analysis role, I can bring data preparation and reconciliation skills. I would like to understand how success is measured and how this role works with Production, Quality and Procurement.\n\n我对这个岗位感兴趣，因为它结合了结构化解决问题和团队协作。统计学背景帮助我认真处理口径和证据。在 AUMOVIO，我整理责任人、日期、状态和风险，支持项目跟踪；数据运营中，我使用 Python 整合跨平台记录并准备一致的报表输出；业务运营中，我核对过 Excel 与 BI 的差异。项目协调方向我能提供清晰的跟踪与跟进，数据分析方向我能提供数据准备和核对能力。我也希望了解岗位成功标准及其与生产、质量、采购的协作方式。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：根据目标岗位选读标准回答中的 PM 或 DA 部分，再回答：What can you contribute in your first few months? 用已有经历支持回答。\n\n写作：根据 W11《岗位面试》的回答原则，给陪练者写90—120词准备邮件：每个例子讲实际职责、个人动作和可核实交付物；支持工作明确说 supported；准备成功标准及生产/质量/采购协作的反问。不要添加录音未提供的面试时间或录用承诺。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [B1 Speaking](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking/b1)：先学 Meeting face-to-face、Agreeing and disagreeing。看视频后替换成自己的工作场景。\n- [Write & Improve](https://writeandimprove.com/)：基础写作练习和自动反馈免费。先独立写首稿，再根据反馈修改；业务事实需另外核查。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W11 听力情境】W11如何说明仅支持过的流程？\n   A. 说成独立负责全部流程\n   B. 明确支持范围并说明可迁移技能\n   C. 删除所有行动细节\n\n2. 【W11 听力情境】哪组面试反问符合录音？\n   A. 成功标准与跨部门协作\n   B. 是否可以省略所有证据\n   C. 客户已保证录用吗\n\n参考答案：1. B，录音强调 supported 的准确范围及技能迁移。；2. A，录音建议问 success measured 和 Production、Quality、Procurement 协作。\n\n## 第12周｜把英语用进完整工作流\n\nMake it work end to end · 共通\n\n学习目标：在陌生情境里独立完成沟通闭环，并确定下一阶段短板。\n\n重点：比较首测与末测的同类任务，既看分数，也看遗漏、用时和独立程度。\n\n表达框架：Understand → Clarify → Explain → Agree → Follow up\n\n### 核心表达\n\n- Here is what we know so far. — 总结当前确认的事实。\n- The remaining uncertainty is … — 指出未决信息。\n- The next action is …, owned by …, due by … — 明确闭环行动。\n\n### 英文示例\n\nAcross my internships, I have worked on data preparation, reconciliation and project tracking. I used Python to organise multi-platform operations data, reviewed differences between Excel and BI outputs, and maintained project status information with owners and planned dates. The common thread is making information easier to check and act on. In a new manufacturing task, I would first confirm the definitions and sources, then summarise what is known and what remains open. I would explain my finding in plain language, identify the person responsible for the next confirmation and keep a written record for follow-up. That is how I would connect my statistics training with practical team needs.\n\n在几段实习中，我做过数据准备、核对与项目跟踪：使用 Python 整理多平台运营数据，复核 Excel 与 BI 差异，以及维护包含责任人与计划日期的项目状态信息。这些工作的共同点是让信息便于核查并落实到行动。面对新的制造业任务，我会先确认口径与来源，再总结已知和未决事项，用清楚的语言解释发现，明确下一次确认的责任人，并保留书面记录以便跟进。这是我把统计训练与团队实际需求连接起来的方式。\n\n### 学习步骤\n\n1. 先听本周录音，核对原文与事实清单。\n2. 学习本章25词，朗读基于简历的标准回答，再脱稿表达。\n3. 使用同一听力材料完成邮件，对照范文修改，最后做章节综合检测。\n\n### 练习任务\n\n口语：用标准回答总结你能带来的工作能力，再基于 W12 模拟材料完成一次2分钟汇报和行动确认。\n\n写作：根据 W12《完整工作流》写100—140词跟进邮件：产量低于计划但缺陷率改善；尚未建立供应与质量变化之间的联系；库存覆盖未知，由计划在下次评审前确认；项目经理随后审议交付选项及审批；记录决定、更新行动表、书面总结。\n\n### 自检\n\n- 能清楚说明真实个人职责\n- 邮件与本周听力事实一致\n- 完成章节综合检测并订正\n\n### 配套学习链接\n\n- [B2 Listening](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening/b2)：先盲听、做题，再看原文。测试保留篇目请在测试中心查看，不提前练。\n- [Write & Improve](https://writeandimprove.com/)：基础写作练习和自动反馈免费。先独立写首稿，再根据反馈修改；业务事实需另外核查。\n- [Manufacturing case studies](https://www.siemens.com/en-us/company/software-case-studies/)：每次只读250—500词，提取 problem / action / result，不必先学会案例中的软件。\n\n### 模块自测（答案在本节最后）\n\n1. 【W12 听力情境】W12生产与质量的状态是？\n   A. 产量达标且缺陷率恶化\n   B. 产量低于计划但缺陷率改善\n   C. 所有指标都改善\n\n2. 【W12 听力情境】谁在下次评审前确认库存覆盖？\n   A. Production Planning\n   B. 已无需任何人确认\n   C. 客户\n\n参考答案：1. B，录音同时陈述产量不足与缺陷率改善，不能混为一谈。；2. A，W12明确由 Production Planning 在 next review 前确认。\n","# 听力模仿与音频使用\n\n## 1. 进入跟读室\n\n[打开听力跟读](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/#audio/1)。每周课程页也提供对应的音频播放器与下载按钮。\n\n12段录音是本站原创脚本的合成示范，使用Microsoft Zira Desktop美式英语声音生成，不是British Council原音，也不是你的真实经历。场景和数字均为模拟。\n\n点击句子编号可以只播放该句。选择0.75×起步，熟悉后回到1×；勾选循环，设置2—5秒留白，留给自己模仿。还可以用A、B按钮标记当前位置，播放自选片段。\n\n## 2. 每天10分钟怎么跟读\n\n1. 整段听一次，不看原稿，用一句话说主旨。\n2. 选2—3句，听清重音、停顿和数字。\n3. 每句模仿两次，尽量维持相同的意群划分，不追求机械复制口音。\n4. 把角色、数量或日期替换，自己说一遍。\n5. 到练习工作台录自己的版本，回听数字、关键词和长停顿。\n\n合成音频方便重复练表达；真实对话的语速、连读、口音变化和临场互动仍用官方材料练习。熟悉的示范不能代替陌生听力测试。\n\n## 3. 音频清单与下载\n\n每个文件都可在播放器的“下载音频”按钮保存。以下为本站原创示范文件：\n\n| 周次 | 场景 | 下载 |\n|---|---|---|\n| W1 | 统计学背景与自我介绍 | [01-introduction.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/01-introduction.wav) |\n| W2 | 面试故事与个人贡献 | [02-interview-story.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/02-interview-story.wav) |\n| W3 | 项目周报 | [03-project-update.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/03-project-update.wav) |\n| W4 | 邮件请求 | [04-email-request.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/04-email-request.wav) |\n| W5 | 数据、百分比与百分点 | [05-data-presentation.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/05-data-presentation.wav) |\n| W6 | 报表口径核实 | [06-data-definitions.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/06-data-definitions.wav) |\n| W7 | 供应协调与审批 | [07-supply-options.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/07-supply-options.wav) |\n| W8 | 会议跟进 | [08-meeting-follow-up.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/08-meeting-follow-up.wav) |\n| W9 | 行业案例与证据 | [09-case-study.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/09-case-study.wav) |\n| W10 | 礼貌异议 | [10-polite-disagreement.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/10-polite-disagreement.wav) |\n| W11 | 岗位面试 | [11-role-interview.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/11-role-interview.wav) |\n| W12 | 综合更新 | [12-complete-update.wav](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/audio/12-complete-update.wav) |\n\n## 4. 用官方原音练习\n\n打开每课的“官方完整课程/查看原文”，在官方页面听音频和读原文。若该课程按其条款提供个人下载，连同原文或练习资料保存；之后可在跟读室点击“选择本地音频”。本地音频可以调速和A—B循环，没有自动对齐的字幕，本站原创句子按钮会暂停使用，以免错误对应。\n\n本机文件保存在当前浏览器IndexedDB，不上传GitHub，不跨设备同步，也不包含在学习记录JSON里。保留原文件作为备份；浏览器限制存储时，仅本次页面可用。\n\n## 5. 为什么不把官方录音直接放到公开仓库\n\n[British Council使用条款](https://www.britishcouncil.org/terms)允许个人非商业学习下载，并要求保留署名和材料限制；未经书面许可限制转载到其他网站，以及脱离课程上下文使用音频直链。因此本站公开提供原创合成录音和完整官方课程链接，不重新托管第三方录音或原文。\n\n本次从官方网页批量提取下载没有成功，页面返回访问限制；没有声称已经下载官方音频。\n","# 每章25词｜职场英语章节词汇手册\n\n12章，每章25个词汇或常用词组，共300个不重复条目。释义与例句为本课程原创教学内容，按制造业项目管理与数据分析场景取义，未列出词语的全部词典义项。\n\n学习入口：https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/1\n\n每天先学5个：理解释义、朗读例句、遮住释义回忆、替换场景造句。标记“再练一次”或“我能使用了”，后者为自评。\n\n测验：章节综合检测27题（25词汇+2同周听力情境，20分钟）；跨章节综合检测25题（20词汇+5情境，20分钟）。词汇题包含英文释义与带中文意图的语境选词。每个词在同一次章节综合检测中只出现一次，选项顺序会随机变化。错词自动进入“需复习”；答对不自动等同掌握。\n\n旧的60分钟听读写说综合评估保留原来的5项权重；章节综合检测单独记录，不把词汇选择题当作口语或写作能力认证。词汇学习状态包含在学习记录JSON导入/导出中。\n\n## W1｜把自己介绍清楚\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/1)\n\n### 01. background\n\nn. 教育或职业背景\n\nMy background is in statistics.\n\n### 02. statistics\n\nn. 统计学\n\nStatistics helps us understand variation in production data.\n\n### 03. graduate\n\nn. 毕业生\n\nThe team is recruiting a graduate for the analyst role.\n\n### 04. candidate\n\nn. 候选人\n\nEach candidate will discuss one relevant project.\n\n### 05. position\n\nn. 职位\n\nI am interested in the project support position.\n\n### 06. qualification\n\nn. 资格；资历\n\nThe job description lists a degree as a required qualification.\n\n### 07. experience\n\nn. 经历；经验\n\nPlease describe your experience with data cleaning.\n\n### 08. responsibility\n\nn. 职责；责任\n\nMy main responsibility was to maintain the tracking list.\n\n### 09. contribution\n\nn. 个人贡献\n\nPlease explain your contribution to the final report.\n\n### 10. skill\n\nn. 技能\n\nClear writing is a useful skill in project work.\n\n### 11. analytical\n\nadj. 善于分析的；分析性的\n\nThe role requires analytical thinking.\n\n### 12. collaborate\n\nv. 协作\n\nWe collaborate with Quality to check the defect data.\n\n### 13. communicate\n\nv. 沟通；传达\n\nPlease communicate the revised schedule to the team.\n\n### 14. manufacturing\n\nn. 制造业；制造过程\n\nI would like to apply my skills in manufacturing.\n\n### 15. department\n\nn. 部门\n\nWhich department owns the production plan?\n\n### 16. colleague\n\nn. 同事\n\nA colleague from Procurement will join the call.\n\n### 17. objective\n\nn. 目标；目的\n\nThe objective is to make delivery risks visible.\n\n### 18. achievement\n\nn. 成果；成就\n\nChoose an achievement that you can support with evidence.\n\n### 19. deliverable\n\nn. 交付物\n\nThe weekly report is the main deliverable for this task.\n\n### 20. reliable\n\nadj. 可靠的\n\nWe need a reliable source for the delivery dates.\n\n### 21. accurate\n\nadj. 准确的\n\nAn accurate summary helps the manager make a decision.\n\n### 22. initiative\n\nn. 主动性\n\nShe showed initiative by checking the missing information.\n\n### 23. adapt\n\nv. 适应；调整\n\nI can adapt my explanation to a non-technical audience.\n\n### 24. strength\n\nn. 优势；长处\n\nOne strength I can demonstrate is careful data checking.\n\n### 25. value\n\nn. 价值\n\nThe analysis adds value by identifying the next action.\n\n## W2｜让经历经得起追问\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/2)\n\n### 01. challenge\n\nn. 挑战；难题\n\nThe main challenge was inconsistent reporting.\n\n### 02. context\n\nn. 背景情况；语境\n\nGive the interviewer enough context to understand the problem.\n\n### 03. task\n\nn. 任务\n\nMy task was to compare the two status reports.\n\n### 04. approach\n\nn. 方法；处理思路\n\nI chose a simple approach that the team could maintain.\n\n### 05. evidence\n\nn. 证据\n\nKeep evidence of how you checked the final figures.\n\n### 06. outcome\n\nn. 结果\n\nThe outcome was a report with clear action owners.\n\n### 07. reflection\n\nn. 反思\n\nMy reflection focused on how to align definitions earlier.\n\n### 08. priority\n\nn. 优先级；优先事项\n\nThe customer deadline was the highest priority.\n\n### 09. deadline\n\nn. 截止期限\n\nWe agreed on a deadline for the first draft.\n\n### 10. ownership\n\nn. 责任归属；担当\n\nClear ownership prevented the issue from being ignored.\n\n### 11. coordinate\n\nv. 协调\n\nI helped coordinate the updates from three departments.\n\n### 12. resolve\n\nv. 解决\n\nWe needed to resolve the difference between the reports.\n\n### 13. implement\n\nv. 实施；执行\n\nThe team agreed to implement the new reporting template.\n\n### 14. demonstrate\n\nv. 展示；证明\n\nUse one specific example to demonstrate your contribution.\n\n### 15. clarify\n\nv. 澄清；说清楚\n\nI asked the owner to clarify the status definition.\n\n### 16. verify\n\nv. 核验；查证\n\nWe used the source records to verify the total.\n\n### 17. assumption\n\nn. 假设；未经证实的前提\n\nI explained the assumption behind the estimate.\n\n### 18. feedback\n\nn. 反馈\n\nThe manager gave feedback on the first draft.\n\n### 19. stakeholder\n\nn. 利益相关方；相关参与方\n\nEach stakeholder needed a different level of detail.\n\n### 20. trade-off\n\nn. 取舍；权衡\n\nWe discussed the trade-off between speed and cost.\n\n### 21. root cause\n\nn. phr. 根本原因\n\nThe team had not confirmed the root cause of the error.\n\n### 22. improvement\n\nn. 改进\n\nThe improvement made the weekly review easier to follow.\n\n### 23. lesson learned\n\nn. phr. 经验教训\n\nOne lesson learned was to confirm definitions before collecting data.\n\n### 24. follow-up\n\nn. 后续跟进\n\nI sent a follow-up after the meeting.\n\n### 25. transferable\n\nadj. 可迁移的\n\nData checking is a transferable skill for project support.\n\n## W3｜做一次有行动的项目周报\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/3)\n\n### 01. milestone\n\nn. 里程碑；关键节点\n\nThe validation milestone is scheduled for next month.\n\n### 02. schedule\n\nn. 日程；进度计划\n\nThe team is reviewing the production schedule.\n\n### 03. timeline\n\nn. 时间线\n\nThe timeline shows the order of the major activities.\n\n### 04. dependency\n\nn. 依赖关系\n\nThe test has a dependency on sample availability.\n\n### 05. progress\n\nn. 进展\n\nPlease give a short update on progress.\n\n### 06. status\n\nn. 当前状态\n\nThe status of the task is still pending.\n\n### 07. on track\n\nphr. 按计划推进\n\nThe assembly task is on track for Friday.\n\n### 08. at risk\n\nphr. 存在无法达成的风险\n\nThe milestone is at risk because one part is missing.\n\n### 09. overdue\n\nadj. 已逾期的\n\nThe overdue action needs an updated completion date.\n\n### 10. action item\n\nn. phr. 行动项\n\nEvery action item needs a named owner.\n\n### 11. owner\n\nn. 责任人\n\nAlex is the owner of the delivery confirmation.\n\n### 12. due date\n\nn. phr. 到期日；应完成日期\n\nPlease add a due date to the action list.\n\n### 13. scope\n\nn. 工作范围\n\nThis change is outside the agreed project scope.\n\n### 14. resource\n\nn. 资源\n\nThe test bench is a limited resource.\n\n### 15. allocation\n\nn. 分配\n\nThe manager will review the allocation of testing time.\n\n### 16. baseline\n\nn. 基准计划；比较基线\n\nCompare the latest schedule with the approved baseline.\n\n### 17. critical path\n\nn. phr. 关键路径\n\nA delay on the critical path can affect the project end date.\n\n### 18. blocker\n\nn. 阻碍推进的问题\n\nThe missing approval is the main blocker.\n\n### 19. escalate\n\nv. 升级处理；上报\n\nWe should escalate the resource conflict to the project manager.\n\n### 20. recovery plan\n\nn. phr. 进度恢复计划\n\nPlease prepare a recovery plan for the delayed task.\n\n### 21. approval\n\nn. 批准；审批\n\nThe change requires approval before implementation.\n\n### 22. commitment\n\nn. 承诺\n\nDo not make a delivery commitment before the review.\n\n### 23. alignment\n\nn. 对齐；达成一致\n\nWe need alignment on the revised priorities.\n\n### 24. completion\n\nn. 完成\n\nThe report should show the expected completion of each task.\n\n### 25. handover\n\nn. 交接\n\nThe handover includes the open issues and action owners.\n\n## W4｜写清一封邮件，跟完一件事\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/4)\n\n### 01. subject\n\nn. 邮件主题\n\nWrite a subject that explains the action needed.\n\n### 02. recipient\n\nn. 收件人\n\nCheck the recipient before sending the email.\n\n### 03. attachment\n\nn. 附件\n\nThe updated plan is included as an attachment.\n\n### 04. enquiry\n\nn. 询问；咨询\n\nI am writing an enquiry about the earliest delivery date.\n\n### 05. request\n\nn. 请求\n\nPlease include a clear request in the first paragraph.\n\n### 06. confirm\n\nv. 确认\n\nCould you confirm the revised delivery date?\n\n### 07. availability\n\nn. 可用时间；可用情况\n\nPlease share your availability for a short call.\n\n### 08. arrange\n\nv. 安排\n\nWe need to arrange a meeting with the supplier.\n\n### 09. reschedule\n\nv. 重新安排时间\n\nCould we reschedule the review for Thursday?\n\n### 10. postpone\n\nv. 推迟\n\nWe may need to postpone the meeting until the data is ready.\n\n### 11. bring forward\n\nv. phr. 将时间提前\n\nCould we bring forward the call to nine in the morning?\n\n### 12. acknowledge\n\nv. 确认收到；知悉\n\nPlease acknowledge receipt of the revised drawing.\n\n### 13. reminder\n\nn. 提醒；催办通知\n\nThis is a reminder that the update is due today.\n\n### 14. update\n\nn. 更新信息\n\nPlease send an update by two in the afternoon.\n\n### 15. reference\n\nn. 参考；参照\n\nThe previous email is attached for reference.\n\n### 16. regarding\n\nprep. 关于\n\nI am writing regarding the component shortage.\n\n### 17. by\n\nprep. 不晚于；截至\n\nPlease reply by noon tomorrow.\n\n### 18. within\n\nprep. 在某段时间之内\n\nPlease respond within two working days.\n\n### 19. pending\n\nadj. 待处理的；待定的\n\nThe quotation is still pending.\n\n### 20. propose\n\nv. 提议\n\nI would like to propose a short review meeting.\n\n### 21. consolidate\n\nv. 汇总；整合\n\nI will consolidate the updates into one report.\n\n### 22. reply\n\nn. 回复\n\nThank you for your prompt reply.\n\n### 23. copy\n\nv. 抄送\n\nPlease copy the project manager on the email.\n\n### 24. agenda\n\nn. 会议议程\n\nThe agenda lists three decisions for discussion.\n\n### 25. minutes\n\nn. 会议纪要\n\nI will send the minutes after the meeting.\n\n## W5｜把数字讲成业务结论\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/5)\n\n### 01. metric\n\nn. 指标\n\nDefine the metric before comparing the results.\n\n### 02. indicator\n\nn. 指示性指标\n\nOn-time delivery is one indicator of service performance.\n\n### 03. output\n\nn. 产出\n\nThe daily output was nine hundred units.\n\n### 04. target\n\nn. 目标值\n\nThe production target was one thousand units.\n\n### 05. actual\n\nadj. 实际的\n\nCompare actual output with the plan.\n\n### 06. variance\n\nn. 差异；统计学中的方差\n\nIn this report, variance means actual output minus planned output.\n\n### 07. percentage\n\nn. 百分比\n\nExpress the completion rate as a percentage.\n\n### 08. percentage point\n\nn. phr. 百分点\n\nA rise from three to four percent is one percentage point.\n\n### 09. relative change\n\nn. phr. 相对变化\n\nThe relative change uses the previous value as its denominator.\n\n### 10. absolute change\n\nn. phr. 绝对变化\n\nThe absolute change in output was one hundred units.\n\n### 11. defect\n\nn. 缺陷\n\nThe inspection found a defect in the housing.\n\n### 12. defect rate\n\nn. phr. 缺陷率\n\nThe defect rate was four percent of the units produced.\n\n### 13. on-time delivery\n\nn. phr. 准时交付；按时交付指标\n\nOn-time delivery fell from ninety-two to eighty-eight percent.\n\n### 14. throughput\n\nn. 单位时间产出；吞吐量\n\nThe line throughput is measured in units per hour.\n\n### 15. trend\n\nn. 趋势\n\nThe chart shows a downward trend in rework.\n\n### 16. increase\n\nn. 增加；上升\n\nThe report shows an increase in completed orders.\n\n### 17. decrease\n\nn. 减少；下降\n\nThere was a decrease in overdue actions.\n\n### 18. fluctuate\n\nv. 波动\n\nWeekly demand can fluctuate during a product launch.\n\n### 19. peak\n\nn. 峰值\n\nThe chart shows a peak in demand in June.\n\n### 20. average\n\nn. 平均值\n\nThe average lead time was ten days.\n\n### 21. median\n\nn. 中位数\n\nThe median is less affected by extreme values than the mean.\n\n### 22. distribution\n\nn. 分布\n\nCheck the distribution before choosing a summary measure.\n\n### 23. denominator\n\nn. 分母\n\nThe denominator should include the eligible orders only.\n\n### 24. numerator\n\nn. 分子\n\nThe numerator counts the orders delivered on time.\n\n### 25. unit\n\nn. 单位\n\nAlways label the unit on the chart.\n\n## W6｜先对齐口径，再解释差异\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/6)\n\n### 01. definition\n\nn. 定义；口径\n\nWe need a shared definition of a completed order.\n\n### 02. reporting period\n\nn. phr. 报告期间\n\nBoth dashboards must use the same reporting period.\n\n### 03. time window\n\nn. phr. 时间窗口\n\nThe time window covers the last seven days.\n\n### 04. granularity\n\nn. 数据粒度\n\nThe granularity of this table is one row per order.\n\n### 05. data source\n\nn. phr. 数据来源\n\nPlease confirm the data source for the dashboard.\n\n### 06. refresh\n\nv. 刷新；更新数据\n\nPlease refresh the dataset before the review.\n\n### 07. missing value\n\nn. phr. 缺失值\n\nA missing value does not always mean zero.\n\n### 08. duplicate\n\nn. 重复记录；重复项\n\nCheck whether the extra row is a duplicate.\n\n### 09. outlier\n\nn. 异常值；离群值\n\nInvestigate the outlier before removing it.\n\n### 10. record\n\nn. 记录\n\nEach record represents one completed order.\n\n### 11. field\n\nn. 字段\n\nThe delivery-date field contains several missing values.\n\n### 12. filter\n\nn. 筛选条件\n\nApply the same filter to both reports.\n\n### 13. join\n\nn. 数据表连接\n\nAn incorrect join can multiply the number of rows.\n\n### 14. key\n\nn. 连接键；标识键\n\nThe order number is the key used to match the tables.\n\n### 15. consistency\n\nn. 一致性\n\nCheck the consistency of the date formats.\n\n### 16. completeness\n\nn. 完整性\n\nWe assessed completeness by checking the required fields.\n\n### 17. validity\n\nn. 有效性；符合规则的程度\n\nThe validity check rejects impossible dates.\n\n### 18. accuracy\n\nn. 准确性\n\nCompare the report with source records to check accuracy.\n\n### 19. reconcile\n\nv. 核对并调节差异\n\nWe need to reconcile the dashboard with the approved report.\n\n### 20. extract\n\nv. 提取数据\n\nPlease extract the orders for the agreed period.\n\n### 21. transform\n\nv. 转换；加工数据\n\nWe transform the date field into a standard format.\n\n### 22. aggregate\n\nv. 汇总；聚合\n\nPlease aggregate the results by production line.\n\n### 23. validate\n\nv. 验证是否满足要求\n\nWe validate the dataset against the agreed rules.\n\n### 24. traceability\n\nn. 可追溯性\n\nTraceability helps us find the source of a reported number.\n\n### 25. version control\n\nn. phr. 版本控制\n\nVersion control prevents the team from using an outdated report.\n\n## W7｜处理供应与验证的冲突\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/7)\n\n### 01. supplier\n\nn. 供应商\n\nThe supplier has not confirmed the shipment date.\n\n### 02. procurement\n\nn. 采购职能；采购部门\n\nProcurement will request a revised quotation.\n\n### 03. inventory\n\nn. 库存\n\nWe need to check inventory before changing the plan.\n\n### 04. stock\n\nn. 存货；现货库存\n\nThe part is currently out of stock.\n\n### 05. shortage\n\nn. 短缺\n\nThe component shortage may affect the next build.\n\n### 06. lead time\n\nn. phr. 交付前置时间；提前期\n\nThe supplier lead time is three weeks.\n\n### 07. shipment\n\nn. 发运；一批发运货物\n\nThe shipment contains two hundred components.\n\n### 08. partial shipment\n\nn. phr. 分批交货；部分发运\n\nA partial shipment could support the initial build.\n\n### 09. expedite\n\nv. 加急；加快处理\n\nWe may need to expedite the delivery after approval.\n\n### 10. quotation\n\nn. 报价单；报价\n\nPlease send a quotation for expedited shipping.\n\n### 11. purchase order\n\nn. phr. 采购订单\n\nThe purchase order lists the agreed quantity.\n\n### 12. capacity\n\nn. 产能；处理能力\n\nThe factory has limited capacity this week.\n\n### 13. production planning\n\nn. phr. 生产计划职能\n\nProduction planning will assess the build sequence.\n\n### 14. validation\n\nn. 验证；适用性确认\n\nValidation must be completed before the release.\n\n### 15. inspection\n\nn. 检验；检查\n\nThe inspection found several nonconforming parts.\n\n### 16. rework\n\nn. 返工\n\nThe damaged units require rework before delivery.\n\n### 17. scrap\n\nn. 报废品；报废材料\n\nWe track scrap separately from rework.\n\n### 18. batch\n\nn. 批次\n\nThe issue affected one batch of components.\n\n### 19. buffer\n\nn. 缓冲；缓冲量\n\nThe schedule includes a small buffer for testing.\n\n### 20. safety stock\n\nn. phr. 安全库存\n\nSafety stock helps cover unexpected demand or supply delays.\n\n### 21. contingency\n\nn. 应急安排；备用措施\n\nWe need a contingency if the shipment is late.\n\n### 22. alternative\n\nn. 替代方案\n\nPlease compare the cost of each alternative.\n\n### 23. substitute\n\nn. 替代品\n\nThe proposed substitute requires technical approval.\n\n### 24. feasibility\n\nn. 可行性\n\nWe need to assess the feasibility of a partial shipment.\n\n### 25. constraint\n\nn. 约束条件\n\nThe main constraint is the available testing time.\n\n## W8｜从讨论到书面闭环\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/8)\n\n### 01. decision\n\nn. 决定；决策\n\nThe decision is recorded in the meeting minutes.\n\n### 02. agreement\n\nn. 约定；一致意见\n\nWe reached an agreement on the next review date.\n\n### 03. proposal\n\nn. 提案；建议方案\n\nThe proposal is still waiting for approval.\n\n### 04. action log\n\nn. phr. 行动项台账\n\nPlease update the action log after the meeting.\n\n### 05. open issue\n\nn. phr. 未解决的问题\n\nThe remaining open issue is the delivery date.\n\n### 06. follow through\n\nv. phr. 将跟进落实到底\n\nWe need to follow through on the agreed actions.\n\n### 07. assign\n\nv. 分派；指派\n\nPlease assign an owner to the new action.\n\n### 08. accountable\n\nadj. 承担最终责任的\n\nThe project manager is accountable for the overall decision.\n\n### 09. consult\n\nv. 征求意见；咨询\n\nWe should consult Quality before changing the inspection plan.\n\n### 10. inform\n\nv. 告知\n\nPlease inform the team of the revised schedule.\n\n### 11. review\n\nv. 审查；评审\n\nWe will review the options at the next checkpoint.\n\n### 12. confirm understanding\n\nv. phr. 确认理解一致\n\nLet us confirm understanding before we end the call.\n\n### 13. summarise\n\nv. 概括；总结\n\nI will summarise the decisions in a short email.\n\n### 14. document\n\nv. 记录成文；形成文档\n\nPlease document the reason for the change.\n\n### 15. circulate\n\nv. 传阅；分发\n\nI will circulate the minutes to the attendees.\n\n### 16. consensus\n\nn. 共识\n\nThe team reached consensus on the priority.\n\n### 17. exception\n\nn. 例外\n\nAny exception to the process needs approval.\n\n### 18. discrepancy\n\nn. 不一致；差异\n\nWe found a discrepancy between the two reports.\n\n### 19. amend\n\nv. 修订\n\nPlease amend the due date in the action log.\n\n### 20. closure\n\nn. 关闭；结项状态\n\nThe issue needs evidence before closure.\n\n### 21. sign-off\n\nn. 正式批准；签核\n\nThe release requires sign-off from the authorised owner.\n\n### 22. escalation\n\nn. 升级处理；上报事项\n\nThe resource conflict requires escalation.\n\n### 23. checkpoint\n\nn. 检查节点\n\nWe will discuss progress at the next checkpoint.\n\n### 24. meeting invite\n\nn. phr. 会议邀请\n\nPlease send an updated meeting invite.\n\n### 25. next step\n\nn. phr. 下一步行动\n\nThe next step is to confirm inventory coverage.\n\n## W9｜读懂一篇制造业案例\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/9)\n\n### 01. case study\n\nn. phr. 案例研究；案例介绍\n\nThe case study describes a quality-management project.\n\n### 02. business need\n\nn. phr. 业务需求\n\nStart by identifying the business need.\n\n### 03. productivity\n\nn. 生产率\n\nThe company measured productivity as output per labour hour.\n\n### 04. efficiency\n\nn. 效率；投入产出效率\n\nThe new schedule improved efficiency by reducing idle time.\n\n### 05. effectiveness\n\nn. 有效性；达成目标的程度\n\nWe assessed effectiveness against the stated objective.\n\n### 06. digitalisation\n\nn. 数字化\n\nDigitalisation can connect information across the factory.\n\n### 07. integration\n\nn. 集成；整合\n\nSystem integration reduced the need for manual copying.\n\n### 08. automation\n\nn. 自动化\n\nThe team used automation for a repetitive reporting task.\n\n### 09. transparency\n\nn. 透明度\n\nThe shared action list improved transparency.\n\n### 10. standardisation\n\nn. 标准化\n\nStandardisation helped the sites use the same definitions.\n\n### 11. implementation\n\nn. 实施过程\n\nThe implementation included training and data checks.\n\n### 12. measurement\n\nn. 测量；衡量\n\nThe article should explain the measurement method.\n\n### 13. benchmark\n\nn. 对标基准\n\nThe team used a comparable line as a benchmark.\n\n### 14. comparison\n\nn. 比较\n\nA fair comparison uses consistent definitions.\n\n### 15. reported outcome\n\nn. phr. 来源所报告的结果\n\nThe reported outcome should be attributed to the case study.\n\n### 16. attribution\n\nn. 来源归属；归因\n\nClear attribution shows where the claim came from.\n\n### 17. independent evidence\n\nn. phr. 独立证据\n\nWe need independent evidence to verify the supplier claim.\n\n### 18. source\n\nn. 来源\n\nPlease cite the source of the reported figure.\n\n### 19. bias\n\nn. 偏差；偏倚\n\nSelection bias can affect which results are reported.\n\n### 20. limitation\n\nn. 局限\n\nOne limitation is the short observation period.\n\n### 21. benefit\n\nn. 收益；益处\n\nExplain the business benefit of the change.\n\n### 22. cost saving\n\nn. phr. 成本节约\n\nThe reported cost saving needs a clear calculation basis.\n\n### 23. quality management\n\nn. phr. 质量管理\n\nThe project aimed to improve quality management.\n\n### 24. process\n\nn. 流程；过程\n\nThe team mapped the process before proposing changes.\n\n### 25. system\n\nn. 系统\n\nThe new system connects production and quality data.\n\n## W10｜提出建议，也能礼貌异议\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/10)\n\n### 01. concern\n\nn. 顾虑；担忧事项\n\nMy concern is that validation will not be complete.\n\n### 02. alternative option\n\nn. phr. 备选方案\n\nCould we consider an alternative option?\n\n### 03. compromise\n\nn. 折中方案；妥协\n\nThe team discussed a compromise on the delivery sequence.\n\n### 04. negotiate\n\nv. 协商；谈判\n\nWe need to negotiate a realistic schedule.\n\n### 05. justify\n\nv. 说明理由；论证合理性\n\nPlease justify the request with evidence.\n\n### 06. rationale\n\nn. 理由；依据\n\nThe rationale for the change should be recorded.\n\n### 07. evaluate\n\nv. 评估；比较判断\n\nWe will evaluate the options against three criteria.\n\n### 08. criterion\n\nn. 评价标准；准则\n\nCost is one criterion for the decision.\n\n### 09. risk assessment\n\nn. phr. 风险评估\n\nThe risk assessment considers likelihood and impact.\n\n### 10. mitigation\n\nn. 风险缓解措施\n\nThe proposed mitigation is to reserve extra testing time.\n\n### 11. impact\n\nn. 影响\n\nWe have not confirmed the impact on customer delivery.\n\n### 12. likelihood\n\nn. 发生可能性\n\nThe team assessed the likelihood of a shortage.\n\n### 13. consequence\n\nn. 后果\n\nA possible consequence is a delayed validation milestone.\n\n### 14. correlation\n\nn. 相关性\n\nCorrelation alone does not establish a causal relationship.\n\n### 15. causation\n\nn. 因果关系\n\nWe need stronger evidence before claiming causation.\n\n### 16. confounder\n\nn. 混杂因素\n\nProduct mix could be a confounder in this comparison.\n\n### 17. uncertainty\n\nn. 不确定性\n\nThe estimate should communicate its uncertainty.\n\n### 18. confidence interval\n\nn. phr. 置信区间\n\nReport the confidence interval alongside the estimate.\n\n### 19. sample size\n\nn. phr. 样本量\n\nThe sample size affects the precision of the estimate.\n\n### 20. statistical significance\n\nn. phr. 统计显著性\n\nStatistical significance alone does not show business value.\n\n### 21. practical significance\n\nn. phr. 实际意义；业务意义\n\nWe should also consider the practical significance of the difference.\n\n### 22. sensitivity analysis\n\nn. phr. 敏感性分析\n\nA sensitivity analysis checks how assumptions affect the result.\n\n### 23. scenario\n\nn. 情景；设定情况\n\nLet us compare the cost under each scenario.\n\n### 24. diplomatic\n\nadj. 得体的；讲究沟通方式的\n\nA diplomatic response can keep the discussion productive.\n\n### 25. constructive\n\nadj. 建设性的\n\nPlease offer a constructive suggestion with your concern.\n\n## W11｜对准你的下一场面试\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/11)\n\n### 01. job description\n\nn. phr. 职位描述\n\nRead the job description before choosing interview examples.\n\n### 02. requirement\n\nn. 要求\n\nMatch each requirement with a relevant piece of evidence.\n\n### 03. essential\n\nadj. 必需的；必要的\n\nThe advertisement lists English communication as essential.\n\n### 04. desirable\n\nadj. 优先考虑的；加分的\n\nManufacturing experience is desirable for this position.\n\n### 05. competency\n\nn. 胜任力\n\nThe interview will assess a specific competency through examples.\n\n### 06. fit\n\nn. 匹配程度\n\nExplain your fit for the role using actual experience.\n\n### 07. relevant\n\nadj. 相关的\n\nChoose a relevant example rather than your longest story.\n\n### 08. portfolio\n\nn. 作品集；成果材料集\n\nMy portfolio includes a report and a dashboard example.\n\n### 09. capability\n\nn. 能力；执行能力\n\nThe task helps demonstrate your analytical capability.\n\n### 10. proficiency\n\nn. 熟练程度\n\nThe role requires proficiency in written English.\n\n### 11. fluency\n\nn. 流利程度\n\nRegular speaking practice can improve fluency.\n\n### 12. exposure\n\nn. 接触经验\n\nI have had exposure to project reporting processes.\n\n### 13. supporting role\n\nn. phr. 支持性角色\n\nI had a supporting role in the weekly review.\n\n### 14. take ownership\n\nv. phr. 主动承担责任\n\nI can take ownership of maintaining the action list.\n\n### 15. availability date\n\nn. phr. 可到岗日期\n\nPlease confirm your availability date with the recruiter.\n\n### 16. onboarding\n\nn. 入职融入；入职培训过程\n\nThe onboarding plan introduces the team and its processes.\n\n### 17. development\n\nn. 发展；培养\n\nI would like to discuss opportunities for professional development.\n\n### 18. expectation\n\nn. 期望；预期要求\n\nAsk about the manager's expectation for the first month.\n\n### 19. performance\n\nn. 绩效；工作表现\n\nHow does the team evaluate performance in this role?\n\n### 20. success measure\n\nn. phr. 成功衡量标准\n\nAsk for a clear success measure for the position.\n\n### 21. cross-functional\n\nadj. 跨职能的\n\nThe position involves cross-functional communication.\n\n### 22. reporting line\n\nn. phr. 汇报关系\n\nCould you explain the reporting line for this role?\n\n### 23. career goal\n\nn. phr. 职业目标\n\nMy career goal connects data analysis with business operations.\n\n### 24. interviewer\n\nn. 面试官\n\nThe interviewer may ask how you verified the result.\n\n### 25. motivation\n\nn. 动机；求职意愿\n\nExplain your motivation for working in manufacturing.\n\n## W12｜把英语用进完整工作流\n\n[在线学习本章词汇](https://lu36366.github.io/work-english-lab/?v=4#vocab/12)\n\n### 01. change request\n\nn. phr. 变更申请\n\nThe new delivery requirement needs a change request.\n\n### 02. change control\n\nn. phr. 变更控制\n\nChange control helps the team assess the effects of a revision.\n\n### 03. contingency plan\n\nn. phr. 应急预案\n\nThe contingency plan explains what to do if supply is interrupted.\n\n### 04. decision log\n\nn. phr. 决策记录台账\n\nThe decision log records the approved option and its rationale.\n\n### 05. acceptance criteria\n\nn. phr. 验收标准\n\nAgree on the acceptance criteria before starting the task.\n\n### 06. delivery commitment\n\nn. phr. 交付承诺\n\nA delivery commitment should follow a feasibility review.\n\n### 07. inventory coverage\n\nn. phr. 库存覆盖能力；可支撑时长\n\nInventory coverage shows how long the available stock can support demand.\n\n### 08. data quality\n\nn. phr. 数据质量\n\nCheck data quality before reporting a change in performance.\n\n### 09. production yield\n\nn. phr. 生产良率；合格产出比例\n\nDefine production yield and its denominator before comparing lines.\n\n### 10. reject rate\n\nn. phr. 不合格品率；拒收率\n\nThe reject rate must use a clearly defined inspection population.\n\n### 11. downtime\n\nn. 停机时间\n\nThe report separates planned downtime from unplanned stops.\n\n### 12. utilisation\n\nn. 利用率\n\nCapacity utilisation depends on the available operating time.\n\n### 13. bottleneck\n\nn. 瓶颈\n\nThe test bench is the bottleneck in the current process.\n\n### 14. corrective action\n\nn. phr. 纠正措施\n\nThe corrective action addresses the cause of the detected problem.\n\n### 15. preventive action\n\nn. phr. 预防措施\n\nThe preventive action addresses a potential problem before it occurs.\n\n### 16. continuous improvement\n\nn. phr. 持续改进\n\nThe team reviews recurring issues as part of continuous improvement.\n\n### 17. forecast\n\nn. 预测\n\nThe demand forecast guides the inventory review.\n\n### 18. estimate\n\nn. 估计值；估算\n\nExplain the assumptions behind the cost estimate.\n\n### 19. assess\n\nv. 评估；判断\n\nWe need to assess the possible delivery impact.\n\n### 20. monitor\n\nv. 监测；持续关注\n\nThe team will monitor the defect rate each week.\n\n### 21. track\n\nv. 跟踪\n\nPlease track the action until the owner confirms completion.\n\n### 22. notify\n\nv. 通知\n\nWe will notify the stakeholders after the decision.\n\n### 23. approve\n\nv. 批准\n\nOnly the authorised manager can approve the extra cost.\n\n### 24. unresolved\n\nadj. 尚未解决的\n\nThe unresolved issue remains on the action list.\n\n### 25. close the loop\n\nv. phr. 完成沟通与行动闭环\n\nWe need to close the loop by confirming the decision and next action.\n"];
